WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.300
Hi there, this is Geshe
Michael Roach and welcome to this

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.110
little talk about the practice

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.250
of The Thousand Angels
of the Heaven of Bliss.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.400
I know you guys have
about another week or two

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.540
before you're going to go into
your 3-day weekend retreat.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.260
I know that you'll be using

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.170
the practice of The Thousand Angels

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.590
in your 3-day retreat

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.980
and I just wanted to talk about it.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.470
We've been through the
steps of it many times

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.690
and we'll talk a little
bit about that today.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:46.180
I think I was trying to remember

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:50.240
the first time I ever
did this practice myself,

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.800
and the time that my
teacher taught it to me.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.343
I remember it was a little bit,

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.650
it felt a little bit strange

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:03.860
because it was some Tibetan guy

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.830
and I was supposed to

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.210
close my eyes and
picture this Tibetan guy.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.500
Of course my teacher had many paintings

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.630
of this ceremony,

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.450
there's Je Tsongkapa

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.120
up in on some clouds

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.630
and then out of,

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:27.950
he's coming out as the heart of Maitreya,

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:32.150
and then I'm supposed to
think about this Tibetan guy

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.960
and imagine that he's coming down.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.720
Then I do all these nice things for him

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.570
and it was very foreign to me.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:46.570
I didn't feel close to the
people that they were describing.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.730
I didn't know Tibetans very well

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:51.873
and recently,

00:01:51.873 --> 00:01:56.200
I was working on a text
about emptiness meditations,

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.430
and somebody asked me,
Veronica, my wife asked me,

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.900
"Well, where did Tibetan come from?"

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.640
You know you're always
talking about Sanskrit

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.630
and how it's says,

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.680
how we can get English
words out of Sanskrit.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.700
Then she said, "I'm just curious about

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.330
where did the Tibetan come from?"

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.143
And I have to say,

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:23.480
I've heard people say it
just dropped out of the sky

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.460
and Tibetans will tell
you something like that,

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:28.420
that it just dropped out of the sky.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:30.880
And then you read, if you go online,

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.970
you'll see people say oh,
it's Burmese, Tibeto-Burmese

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:37.815
language group but that
doesn't really help.

00:02:37.815 --> 00:02:40.903
It just spread a little
bit in towards Burma.

00:02:42.753 --> 00:02:47.753
It really does seem that had
just dropped out of the sky.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:52.940
Linguistically, it's
not related to anything

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.710
in the world that I know of.

00:02:55.970 --> 00:03:00.660
It really does seem like
it's from another planet.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.943
I spent the last two days in a hospital,

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:09.470
a friend of mine is
undergoing some difficulties.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:12.077
A couple of friends of mine

00:03:12.077 --> 00:03:15.060
have got some serious illnesses

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.830
and they've asked me to help them.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:22.480
And it got me thinking about

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.653
this world

00:03:23.653 --> 00:03:27.613
and these are people who are close to me.

00:03:27.613 --> 00:03:31.493
And one of them is not close to me,

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.710
but they heard about me and they asked,

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:38.200
they keep writing me
letters, emails, about

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.320
what's going to happen to them.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.320
Then I was thinking about it myself

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:49.060
and how to explain it to them.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.800
And I think at a certain age,

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.610
if you spend a lot of time
around people who are dying,

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:58.060
who are seriously ill,

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:02.630
and they trust you and
they're asking you for advice

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:05.060
and they're like, what's
going to happen to me

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.330
and what's it going to be like?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:11.675
I think only when you have someone

00:04:11.675 --> 00:04:16.437
talk to you, your phone
just did a clunky thing.

00:04:16.437 --> 00:04:19.611
(indistinct chatter)

00:04:19.611 --> 00:04:21.600
(Geshe-la laughing)

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.567
Yeah, that's from another world too.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.590
Then,

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:33.000
something happened to
me in the last few days

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:38.000
and that I just became really
aware of different realms.

00:04:38.459 --> 00:04:42.440
I've been trying to explain to someone

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:45.460
what's going to happen
to them when they die.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:49.353
When you think about
someone leaving this world,

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.850
then this world becomes, I don't know,

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:55.720
in my mind it becomes like a pocket,

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:58.500
or some kind of a pocket,

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:03.500
and there's other worlds,
other pockets around it,

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.760
and there's little,

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:10.040
almost like submarine
hatches between the pockets.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:12.900
Then you die in this pocket

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.010
and then you're going to go
through one of those hatches

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:18.170
to a different pocket that we can't see.

00:05:19.292 --> 00:05:22.750
Then I don't know if
I'll ever see you again

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:24.940
anytime soon

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:30.050
because there's probably
millions of pockets like that

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:34.270
and you're going to go through
a small hatch or doorway

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:37.200
and you're going to pass
to a different pocket,

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.900
a different reality,

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.370
and we may not see each other again.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:46.063
Like there's no reason to
think there's just one world,

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:48.850
there are many, many worlds,

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:53.850
and they may touch each
other like eggs in a carton

00:05:54.119 --> 00:05:58.520
but they're completely
separate and they're different.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:02.220
And you will go to a different world

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.840
and there will be different things there,

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.710
and different people there.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.090
It may be completely different

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:10.920
from the world you're in now

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:13.593
and you can go there any time.

00:06:13.593 --> 00:06:16.290
One of the people who's been writing me,

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:18.250
who is not a Buddhist,

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.450
and they're not interested in Buddhism,

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:22.030
but they are dying.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:26.130
They found out about
me through a relative.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:31.130
They were a strong, a healthy, young,

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:35.250
successful filmmaker, very famous,

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.880
in his field

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:40.940
and then just suddenly he's
got some kind of terrible

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:45.190
stomach cancer and they say,
he'll die in a few months.

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:49.680
And he just, he has a beautiful
son and a beautiful wife

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.456
and they're both filmmakers.

00:06:52.456 --> 00:06:55.040
He's asking me what's going to happen?

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.260
Where am I going to go?

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:00.573
And it's kind of,

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:03.610
it's kind of interesting that he,

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:06.780
I don't know, for some reason
he thinks I can tell him.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.780
Then he's really being
good about listening to me.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:13.763
So it's kind of,

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:17.920
sometimes I've had that in my life where

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:19.360
someone will come to me and say,

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:22.990
I have a terrible disease
and only have a few weeks

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:24.800
and can you help me?

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:28.278
They're almost the best
students, right JB?

00:07:28.278 --> 00:07:30.760
Beause they really listen

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.680
and they really do what you tell them.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:36.133
So I'm trying to get you in the mood of,

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:44.440
somehow these Tibetan things came to us

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.300
and even as a language,

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:49.860
it seems that they dropped
out of another world.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:54.410
Like all of these teachings
that we have in Tibetan language

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.680
just dropped out of another world,

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.880
and that John Brady and his team,

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:01.930
I mean, today, they're working on grants.

00:08:03.296 --> 00:08:07.890
I'm trying to push them to
break into another library

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:11.470
in Mongolia that has 300,000 books there.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:14.410
And it's just like, I can't stand it

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:15.980
to think that those books are there

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:17.690
and they might burn up tomorrow

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:19.870
or like something might happen.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:21.880
It just drives me crazy,

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:25.700
like, wow, we have to
try to get those books.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:29.420
Then I think about those books

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:32.422
and they also seem to
be from another world.

00:08:32.422 --> 00:08:37.422
It just seems like they're
not from this normal world.

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:42.830
They're unique. Those
books are very unique.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.520
So why am I talking about that?

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:48.680
The practice of The Thousand Angels,

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:53.680
it's kind of like you're trying
to open up a little doorway

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:57.960
to another world.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.600
I have to say something about Tibetans

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.380
that maybe you don't know.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:08.900
I've lived with Tibetans for 25 years

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.690
and I was surprised about some things:

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:17.080
One is that

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:21.520
as a country,

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:23.880
they're are not different
from any other country. Okay?

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:26.970
I'm sorry to say that

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:32.220
but there's no big
difference between Tibet,

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:34.460
and America, and Russia, and India,

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:37.970
and China. There's not a big difference.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:42.760
The country as a country
is not much different.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:45.910
I was very, what do you call it?,

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:49.640
kind of disappointed. I was disappointed

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:52.860
when I got to know normal Tibetan people.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.940
I started talking with them
and seeing how they live,

00:09:56.940 --> 00:10:01.633
and they're just about
like everybody else.

00:10:01.633 --> 00:10:06.633
There's good people.
There's really bad people.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:09.400
There's greedy people.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:12.110
There were wars.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.230
There was terrible

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:17.010
killing and hurting people.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:21.290
And it's not different
from Europe or America,

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:26.290
or it's not different, the
people are basically the same.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:30.530
But they have this one doorway

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:32.260
to another world

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:35.060
and I don't know why, it
just came through Tibet.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:39.670
So, I mean, if you ever have
to live in Tibetan society

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:43.290
and deal closely with
Tibetan, even in a monastery,

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:45.330
it's disappointing.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.580
They're just pretty normal

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.340
and they have the same kind of

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:56.340
very sad things going on there
that go on every place else.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:02.650
But there's this one doorway that

00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:06.170
they learned how to open and that's,

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:09.570
to me, we're talking about Tsongkapa.

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:11.460
So, I mean, even the name Tsongkapa

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:14.640
when I started to learn about Tsongkapa,

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:16.690
it was very uncomfortable.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:17.800
I'm like,

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:20.732
and they can't even agree
how to spell it right, John?

00:11:20.732 --> 00:11:23.960
Everyone wants to spell
it a different way.

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:27.133
I mean, nobody's name
starts with TZ anywhere.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:33.600
It's just weird, and it's hard
to remember when you're new

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:34.890
to remember that name

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:38.063
and why didn't they call
him John or something easy?

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:44.170
It's just Tsongkapa.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:48.733
It felt strange and foreign
to me when I first learned it.

00:11:48.733 --> 00:11:50.750
It felt kind of

00:11:51.886 --> 00:11:55.960
distant like I would never be able to,

00:11:55.960 --> 00:12:00.960
I couldn't see that I felt
too close to this person

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:04.690
and I didn't feel that attracted to them.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:08.720
My teacher was insisting

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:13.250
that I should try to
learn about Tsongkapa,

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.020
and study about Tsongkapa,

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:16.830
and read Tsongkapa's books,

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:20.070
and I should try to get
a personal relationship

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:20.990
with Tsongkapa,

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:25.260
which is what you're trying
to do in these three days.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:29.590
You're trying to get a
personal relationship

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:33.200
with Tsongkapa. I just want to say,

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:34.910
I don't know where you're from,

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:36.783
Russia, China, wherever you're from,

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:43.500
Mexico, but it's weird there's
somebody named Tsongkapa.

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:46.750
They wear strange clothes.

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:51.570
It's not something easy to relate to.

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:54.090
It's not something from our culture.

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:55.710
It's a totally different thing.

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.670
Then I struggled with that

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:00.330
and I'll be honest about it.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:03.150
In the first few years that I spent

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:05.870
in this small Mongolian monastery,

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:10.092
I struggled with that and
I didn't feel very close to

00:13:10.092 --> 00:13:12.850
Tsongkapa. It was very foreign

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.570
and I didn't know much about him.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:17.560
All I heard was he wrote a lot of books

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:20.160
and there were complicated and difficult.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.950
I wasn't attracted to it,

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:29.280
but the point of this practice is that--

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.140
I can tell a story of Tsongkapa.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:36.353
And Tim, you got an image I think,

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:39.340
the first one, maybe.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:41.270
Yeah, this is a nice story

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:43.853
I think the DCI people know it.

00:13:48.157 --> 00:13:53.150
So Tsongkapa wanted to have a relationship

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:56.360
with Manjushri. And Manjushri, again,

00:13:56.360 --> 00:14:00.510
that's some kind of foreign
word, and foreign name,

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:02.750
and foreign person,

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:05.640
and I remember trying to learn his name,

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:10.240
and all the Westerners in my
class already knew his name

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.150
and I didn't.

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:13.280
I felt uncomfortable
that they knew his name

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:16.240
and I didn't know his name
so they must know who he is

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:18.280
but I don't know who he is.

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:21.910
Everybody would say, oh, he's the

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.230
god of wisdom.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:25.280
I'm like, well, what's the god of wisdom?

00:14:26.346 --> 00:14:30.630
And so Tsongkapa is,

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:34.035
I think he's the person with
his hands like this [in prayer]

00:14:34.035 --> 00:14:35.980
in the middle.

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:40.620
He wants to meet Manjushri.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:44.790
So he heard that Manjushri
understands emptiness

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:47.640
and he really wants to meet him.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:51.010
He's kind of not like you and me,

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:54.590
like Tsongkapa's not thinking,

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:59.240
oh, I would like to meet a teacher

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.750
who can explain about Manjushri to me.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:03.750
He's not thinking like that.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:08.750
He's thinking, well, if the
source from another world

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:12.330
about emptiness teachings is Manjushri

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:14.040
- -this is so Tsongkapa--

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.558
then I want to to meet him myself.

00:15:16.558 --> 00:15:19.283
Just tell me where he lives

00:15:19.283 --> 00:15:21.170
then I'll get in touch with him.

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:26.170
I don't need you guys to
tell me what Manjushri said.

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:31.433
So he goes around asking everybody.

00:15:32.476 --> 00:15:37.330
I'm glad you're offering me
classes. I appreciate it.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:40.330
I've learned a lot but
could I just talk to

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:41.913
Manjushri directly?

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:46.307
And then everybody says, well,

00:15:46.307 --> 00:15:48.147
that takes the years of practice.

00:15:48.147 --> 00:15:51.183
He says, well, is there
anybody who actually did it?

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:55.770
That's the kind of dumb,

00:15:56.820 --> 00:16:00.400
smart question that new people will ask

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.730
and later when you get more
experienced, you stop asking.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:06.561
But I think you should ask.

00:16:06.561 --> 00:16:10.330
He said, well, can I
just meet him directly?

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:14.336
Then somebody said, well,
there is a guy who met

00:16:14.336 --> 00:16:17.420
Manjushri. There is such a person.

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:20.110
Then he says, well,
just tell me his address

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:21.800
and I'll go talk to him.

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:24.620
They're like, he doesn't have an address.

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:26.970
He's like, what do you mean
doesn't have an address?

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:31.600
He's up on the Sedona mountain somewhere.

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:34.050
He's wandering around
with a bunch of sheep.

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:36.000
He doesn't have a house.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:38.640
He just keeps sheep in the mountains.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.130
If you go wander around the mountains,

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:41.940
you might run into him.

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:43.200
It's so funny, right?

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:45.810
Like just there's one
mountain, there's another one,

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:48.083
there's another. Good luck.

00:16:48.083 --> 00:16:52.450
He says, well, okay, what's his name?

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:54.047
They say, Umapa,

00:16:55.810 --> 00:16:59.940
which kind of means
Master of the Middle Way.

00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:02.670
His name means kind of
Master of the Middle Way,

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:03.970
but he's a sheep herder.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:08.997
So Tsongkapa's like, okay,
let me go try to find him.

00:17:08.997 --> 00:17:11.973
And that picture, Tim, you got it?

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:16.970
They should've put it in a,

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:19.350
they should have put it in a
meadow on a mountain somewhere

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:24.010
but anyway, Tsongkapa meets Umapa,

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:26.213
and he says,

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:32.400
I heard that you got direct
contact with Manjushri

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:36.720
and I heard that you can
talk to him directly.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:38.820
And Umapa says,

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.749
yeah, I just imagine he's like,

00:17:40.749 --> 00:17:43.197
- yep, I got that,

00:17:43.197 --> 00:17:44.940
because he's probably no teeth,

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:47.520
he's just a sheep herder
up in the mountains.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:52.170
- -Yeah, yeah, yeah, I'm direct
contact, yeah, that's me.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:54.263
And so Tsongkapa is like,

00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:58.813
- -Do you mind if we just confirmed this?

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:01.740
Can you put the picture back?

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:04.700
This is the moment of confirmation.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:05.533
Tsongkapa says,

00:18:05.533 --> 00:18:09.870
look, I'll ask you
questions about emptiness

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:10.703
and then

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:15.830
you ask Manjushri what he thinks.

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:18.140
I'll ask you some
difficult questions I have

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:20.250
and then you talk to Manjushri

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:22.480
and then I'll judge from your answers

00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:24.870
whether you're in contact
with Manjushri or not.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:27.750
So we, unfortunately we
don't have the questions.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:29.050
It would make a good movie.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:34.470
So he starts asking questions

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:39.400
and then Umapa tarts answering.
And the answers are perfect.

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:41.560
The answers are totally perfect.

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:43.230
Then Tsongkapa was like,

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:47.460
oh my God, you really are
in contact with Manjushri.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:49.330
Then of course,

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:51.070
he writes down all the answers.

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:55.447
He incorporates them into
some of his greatest books

00:18:55.447 --> 00:18:58.520
on emptiness.

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:01.390
Then he gets kind of
impatient and he says, well,

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:04.350
how about I just talk
to Manjushri directly?

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:08.151
Can you introduce me to Manjushri?

00:19:08.151 --> 00:19:11.163
Umapa says it doesn't work like that.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:14.430
You don't have the karma.

00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:18.540
You don't have the seeds to see Manjushri.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:21.890
You can't just ask me to
introduce you to Manjushri,

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.750
it won't work.

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:27.377
He could be sitting next to
you; he is sitting next to you.

00:19:27.377 --> 00:19:31.040
And you can't see him because
you don't have the seeds.

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:33.160
So it's not like

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:34.860
I can make an introduction,

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:39.770
you have to make the seeds.
You have to collect the seeds

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:44.770
to meet him and then
everything will be awesome.

00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:48.240
Then you can, it'll really be awesome.

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:50.800
So I encourage you to make the seeds.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:53.090
And he helped him to make the seeds.

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:55.230
The biggest seed of all

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:58.280
is to realize that it takes
seeds to meet Manjushri.

00:19:58.280 --> 00:19:59.130
That's all.

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:02.200
The biggest seed to
meet Manjushri directly

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:08.210
is to understand emptiness enough

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:11.940
to understand that Manjushri
is coming from you.

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:16.860
So if you really want to meet Manjushri,

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:20.180
you can. You just have to plant the seeds.

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:22.470
The most powerful seed

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:23.767
is to believe you can.

00:20:25.246 --> 00:20:28.942
BTAGS PA'I RNAL 'BYOR -- What's that mean?

00:20:28.942 --> 00:20:29.775
$500.

00:20:32.667 --> 00:20:35.820
(indistinct chatter)

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:38.490
Tim got it, $500.

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:40.877
Collect from Elly I think,

00:20:40.877 --> 00:20:42.123
$500 for the young man.

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:48.650
BTAGS PA'I RNAL 'BJOR means,

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:52.320
it starts by believing
that it could happen.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:56.330
You just kind of pretend
that it could happen.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.610
And Tsongkapa does it.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.677
Why are we talking about that?

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:04.810
We're supposed to be talking about

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:07.160
the practice of The Thousand Angels

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:10.964
and trying to make contact with Tsongkapa.

00:21:10.964 --> 00:21:14.900
Again, what I want to say is

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:16.910
that for me,

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:20.670
I'm stuck in this little
Mongolian temple in New Jersey

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.280
and here's these people
talking about this guy

00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:25.610
whose name I can't pronounce.

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.050
And they're trying to prove to me

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:29.260
that this is going to save my life

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:31.840
and I never heard of him at Princeton.

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:33.270
And I'm like,

00:21:35.693 --> 00:21:37.540
"Are you sure, you know?

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:41.960
Then Rinpoche taught me
the DGA' LDAN LHA BRGYA MA

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:44.370
The Thousand Angels Practice.

00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:48.040
These are seven, eight steps that you do

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:52.890
before a meditation practice.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:56.610
It's called BSAGS SBYANG

00:21:56.610 --> 00:21:58.860
Say BSAGS SBYANG

00:21:58.860 --> 00:22:00.553
And you guys know BSAGS SBYANG,

00:22:00.553 --> 00:22:04.410
I think, BSAGS collect good, new karma.

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:07.380
The word TSOGS comes from BSAGS.

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:10.270
So when you do your TSOGS twice a month,

00:22:10.270 --> 00:22:14.320
by assembling great
quantities of offerings,

00:22:14.320 --> 00:22:16.900
which is called TSOGS, TSOGS-ing them,

00:22:16.900 --> 00:22:17.970
that's called BSAGS.

00:22:17.970 --> 00:22:19.340
Then SBYANG means like,

00:22:19.340 --> 00:22:21.710
GSO SBYONG comes from SBYANG,

00:22:21.710 --> 00:22:25.500
which means to confess your bad deeds.

00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:30.500
So the whole practice
of The Thousand Angels

00:22:30.600 --> 00:22:33.062
is to BSAGS SBYANG.

00:22:33.062 --> 00:22:38.062
On one hand, you want to try to accumulate

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:40.790
a big pile of good seeds,

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:45.600
and then SBYANG means
you want to clean away

00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:47.720
a big pile of bad seeds.

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:49.183
If you're do enough

00:22:51.080 --> 00:22:53.140
collecting new seeds

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:56.900
and if you get rid of enough bad seeds,

00:22:56.900 --> 00:23:01.740
then the door opens to another realm

00:23:01.740 --> 00:23:05.050
and Tsongkapa shows up in your life,

00:23:05.050 --> 00:23:06.437
personally in your life.

00:23:06.437 --> 00:23:07.270
You see?

00:23:07.270 --> 00:23:09.390
So the purpose of

00:23:09.390 --> 00:23:13.550
this ritual is to make contact,

00:23:13.550 --> 00:23:16.060
direct contact with Tsongkapa

00:23:16.060 --> 00:23:18.100
the way he did with Manjushri.

00:23:18.100 --> 00:23:20.820
So you're trying to
get the portal to open.

00:23:20.820 --> 00:23:25.820
It's a lot easier if
you know how it works.

00:23:28.870 --> 00:23:33.690
It's not that Tsongkapa's
waiting for you to ask politely,

00:23:34.760 --> 00:23:39.760
or Tsongkapa refuses to
come to your meditation room

00:23:40.830 --> 00:23:43.900
if you don't do The Thousand Angels

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:45.640
a thousand times at first,

00:23:45.640 --> 00:23:47.840
and then on the thousandth
time, he'll come.

00:23:47.840 --> 00:23:49.117
It's not like that.

00:23:49.117 --> 00:23:51.363
It feels like that when you're new,

00:23:52.870 --> 00:23:54.020
when you're just starting.

00:23:54.020 --> 00:23:57.220
It feels like, okay, I'm going
to have to do 500 of these

00:23:57.220 --> 00:23:59.620
or I'm going to have to do 600 of these,

00:23:59.620 --> 00:24:03.100
and then maybe Tsongkapa will be happy

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:05.130
and come visit me, you know?

00:24:05.130 --> 00:24:06.513
But it's not like that.

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:12.800
It's that you have to open the door

00:24:12.850 --> 00:24:14.780
to get him to come

00:24:14.780 --> 00:24:18.381
and you open the door by doing the ritual,

00:24:18.381 --> 00:24:20.203
by repeating this ritual.

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:23.550
And I'll be honest,

00:24:23.550 --> 00:24:27.920
I just did it out of respect
for my teacher. He said,

00:24:27.920 --> 00:24:32.780
do this practice and I
was not attracted to it

00:24:32.780 --> 00:24:35.520
and I didn't see much point to it.

00:24:35.520 --> 00:24:39.910
I waited a long time
before I did my retreats

00:24:39.910 --> 00:24:41.600
because I wasn't attracted to it.

00:24:41.600 --> 00:24:44.890
I just thought it was
kind of superstitious

00:24:46.055 --> 00:24:47.994
and I thought just

00:24:47.994 --> 00:24:50.236
,DGA' LDAN LHA BRGYA'I
MGON GYI THUGS KA NAS,

00:24:50.236 --> 00:24:51.785
,RAB DKAR ZHO GSAR SPUNGS
'DRA'I CHU 'DZIN RTZER,

00:24:51.785 --> 00:24:53.235
,CHOS KYI RGYAL PO KUN
MKHYEN BLO BZANG GRAGS,

00:24:53.235 --> 00:24:54.851
,SRAS DANG BCAS PA GNAS
'DIR GSHEGS SU GSOL,

00:24:54.851 --> 00:24:58.107
I'll go, okay, I recited it 25 times

00:24:58.107 --> 00:24:59.460
and nothing happened.

00:24:59.460 --> 00:25:04.170
I just felt it was kind of artificial

00:25:05.616 --> 00:25:10.616
but if you can get into
the actual practice,

00:25:12.810 --> 00:25:14.970
then Tsongkapa does come

00:25:16.620 --> 00:25:18.130
and he's cool.

00:25:18.130 --> 00:25:20.560
So I know he has a strange name,

00:25:20.560 --> 00:25:23.530
I think Je Rinpoche
might be easier, right?

00:25:23.530 --> 00:25:24.820
This call him Je Rinpoche,

00:25:24.820 --> 00:25:26.900
that's his other name,

00:25:26.900 --> 00:25:29.647
which means precious one
or something like that.

00:25:31.810 --> 00:25:34.090
But I just want to encourage you

00:25:35.400 --> 00:25:37.990
to do the practice

00:25:37.990 --> 00:25:41.330
because if you do it in a relaxed,

00:25:41.330 --> 00:25:44.866
happy, creative way,

00:25:44.866 --> 00:25:49.070
the door does open to another realm

00:25:49.070 --> 00:25:51.040
and he comes,

00:25:51.040 --> 00:25:54.830
and he starts talking in your head

00:25:54.830 --> 00:25:56.883
and it's really cool.

00:25:58.120 --> 00:26:03.120
So, you can meet those people

00:26:03.160 --> 00:26:04.690
and he is amazing.

00:26:04.690 --> 00:26:08.200
So let's talk about Tsongkapa.

00:26:10.870 --> 00:26:12.383
We just finished, right?,

00:26:13.840 --> 00:26:16.250
editing a book about him.

00:26:16.250 --> 00:26:18.650
We wrote a book,

00:26:18.650 --> 00:26:21.690
I don't know, 20 years ago.

00:26:21.690 --> 00:26:23.620
We translated a book about his life

00:26:24.660 --> 00:26:28.270
and we made a big thick, expensive book

00:26:28.270 --> 00:26:32.870
as a fundraiser to help this
little Mongolian temple.

00:26:32.870 --> 00:26:35.940
And we sold all the books finally

00:26:35.940 --> 00:26:38.040
and I think it was a
hundred thousand dollars.

00:26:38.040 --> 00:26:41.110
We gave all the money to the temple.

00:26:41.110 --> 00:26:44.080
We saved some money to
print the book again.

00:26:44.080 --> 00:26:48.870
Recently we were editing the book.

00:26:48.870 --> 00:26:51.570
We're cleaning it up to make it into a,

00:26:51.570 --> 00:26:54.580
now that we thought all the copies

00:26:54.580 --> 00:26:56.160
to help the temple,

00:26:56.160 --> 00:27:01.160
we were making paperback,
a big paperback book,

00:27:01.430 --> 00:27:05.090
coffee table book, and
we'll be releasing it,

00:27:05.090 --> 00:27:06.409
I think, on, on new year's party?

00:27:06.409 --> 00:27:08.510
(indistinct chatter)

00:27:08.510 --> 00:27:10.326
At the, Insha Allah,

00:27:10.326 --> 00:27:13.730
at the new year's party in Singapore.

00:27:13.730 --> 00:27:17.300
Let's talk about that book.

00:27:17.300 --> 00:27:20.770
In the book,

00:27:20.770 --> 00:27:23.790
you can read,

00:27:23.790 --> 00:27:26.480
basically,

00:27:26.480 --> 00:27:28.370
the biography of his life

00:27:29.440 --> 00:27:33.353
is a story about writing books.

00:27:34.490 --> 00:27:37.440
So here's this great master

00:27:37.440 --> 00:27:40.940
and he did do other
things than write books.

00:27:40.940 --> 00:27:44.020
He went into deep retreats

00:27:44.020 --> 00:27:48.830
and there's a beautiful
painting of him in a KO BA,

00:27:48.830 --> 00:27:49.800
KO BA means

00:27:52.349 --> 00:27:54.640
a leather coracle in English.

00:27:54.640 --> 00:27:59.640
It's a boat made of a
skin of a vaca, of a cow,

00:27:59.910 --> 00:28:02.820
and it must be scary, I don't know.

00:28:02.820 --> 00:28:04.860
They don't have bridges in Tibet

00:28:04.860 --> 00:28:08.540
and they have the most rivers
of anywhere in the world,

00:28:08.540 --> 00:28:09.810
the most streams.

00:28:09.810 --> 00:28:11.280
You can't walk five miles

00:28:11.280 --> 00:28:13.530
without crossing a couple of rivers.

00:28:13.530 --> 00:28:17.160
So you jump in one of these
little personal boats.

00:28:17.160 --> 00:28:20.280
It's round and then
somebody pushes you over

00:28:20.280 --> 00:28:23.000
and then you get out and you keep going.

00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:25.950
So there's a beautiful picture of him

00:28:25.950 --> 00:28:28.730
and his eight closest disciples

00:28:29.830 --> 00:28:31.840
going to YAR MO KLUNG, which is a place

00:28:31.840 --> 00:28:34.250
that he did a retreat.

00:28:34.250 --> 00:28:36.690
There's also a picture,
Tim, you got it there.

00:28:36.690 --> 00:28:38.973
It's I think it's the
last picture you have.

00:28:42.020 --> 00:28:44.893
And before he went to retreat,

00:28:46.260 --> 00:28:49.120
he was having some physical problems.

00:28:49.120 --> 00:28:51.780
And I think that's kind of encouraging

00:28:51.780 --> 00:28:54.700
that Tsongkapa had physical problems.

00:28:54.700 --> 00:28:58.010
He had bad back, he had a bad back.

00:28:58.010 --> 00:29:00.060
His whole life he had a bad back

00:29:00.060 --> 00:29:01.970
and it was hard for him to meditate,

00:29:01.970 --> 00:29:04.240
and it was hard for him to do retreat.

00:29:04.240 --> 00:29:07.840
Here he's meeting a yoga master,

00:29:07.840 --> 00:29:10.610
and he's offering him a mandala.

00:29:10.610 --> 00:29:15.110
I think that's very
important in your retreat.

00:29:15.110 --> 00:29:18.360
When you do your three-day retreat

00:29:18.360 --> 00:29:20.813
or a three-year retreat,

00:29:20.813 --> 00:29:23.863
I've been having fun,
doing yoga with Connie,

00:29:25.200 --> 00:29:27.360
the Director of Yoga Studies Institute,

00:29:27.360 --> 00:29:29.135
and John Brday,

00:29:29.135 --> 00:29:31.470
every day, we've been doing yoga together

00:29:31.470 --> 00:29:34.420
and it's a great practice.

00:29:34.420 --> 00:29:38.830
So if you're going to do
this three-day retreat,

00:29:38.830 --> 00:29:42.910
I really encourage you,
do what Tsongkapa did

00:29:42.910 --> 00:29:45.350
and take care of your health.

00:29:45.350 --> 00:29:48.360
You got to have a physical body

00:29:48.360 --> 00:29:51.230
to do The Thousand Angel practice.

00:29:51.230 --> 00:29:53.930
And to make contact with Tsongkapa,

00:29:53.930 --> 00:29:56.090
you have to have a healthy, physical body.

00:29:56.090 --> 00:29:58.790
So you have to take good care of your body

00:29:58.790 --> 00:30:01.140
and you only get one.

00:30:01.140 --> 00:30:03.450
So it's a really important every day

00:30:03.450 --> 00:30:06.870
to do some physical practices,

00:30:06.870 --> 00:30:10.310
and to eat carefully,
and to get enough sleep,

00:30:10.310 --> 00:30:13.240
that helps you open the door.

00:30:13.240 --> 00:30:16.820
So you do see other,

00:30:16.820 --> 00:30:20.010
a lot of other paintings

00:30:20.010 --> 00:30:22.430
of Tsongkapa doing different things,

00:30:22.430 --> 00:30:27.430
but the main thing was writing
books and studying books.

00:30:28.050 --> 00:30:30.260
I want to tell you a story of a book

00:30:30.260 --> 00:30:32.150
I'm working on right now.

00:30:32.150 --> 00:30:37.150
So I'm in a group of
translators called Mixed Nuts

00:30:38.180 --> 00:30:42.730
and we decided to try to translate

00:30:42.730 --> 00:30:45.770
the most, maybe the twenty,
most important books

00:30:47.520 --> 00:30:51.310
in the world from ancient Buddhism.

00:30:51.310 --> 00:30:56.310
So I got like ten fools, including Seiji,

00:30:57.460 --> 00:31:00.602
what do you call in Spanish?

00:31:01.919 --> 00:31:05.175
Locos. Personas Locos.

00:31:05.175 --> 00:31:06.092
And I said,

00:31:08.100 --> 00:31:11.540
let's translate the twenty greatest books

00:31:11.540 --> 00:31:13.620
of a Buddhism together,

00:31:13.620 --> 00:31:15.420
and some of the Mixed Nuts

00:31:15.420 --> 00:31:19.690
had no experience in
Tibet and translation.

00:31:19.690 --> 00:31:22.550
Like Seiji, like zero,

00:31:22.550 --> 00:31:25.813
he didn't know any words and I
said, well, let's just start.

00:31:26.920 --> 00:31:30.670
So we've been working
really, really, really hard

00:31:31.940 --> 00:31:34.300
for five years,

00:31:34.300 --> 00:31:39.300
and there's about ten main translators

00:31:39.970 --> 00:31:44.500
and they all have a very
difficult book to translate,

00:31:44.500 --> 00:31:45.720
and they're all struggling.

00:31:45.720 --> 00:31:50.250
I'm really amazed and grateful
that no one has quit yet.

00:31:52.140 --> 00:31:53.983
So I don't know why.

00:31:55.690 --> 00:31:58.040
I don't have a good record in the past.

00:31:58.040 --> 00:32:00.840
Most of the people who learned
to translate with me quit,

00:32:03.500 --> 00:32:06.960
but none of these ten people has quit,

00:32:06.960 --> 00:32:09.900
which means intense amount of work for me,

00:32:09.900 --> 00:32:11.680
like hundreds of hours of work.

00:32:11.680 --> 00:32:13.103
Just the classes are,

00:32:14.660 --> 00:32:18.783
just the classes and the
class preparation is,

00:32:18.783 --> 00:32:21.410
I have five, six hundred hours of work

00:32:21.410 --> 00:32:24.420
and it's intense.

00:32:24.420 --> 00:32:29.420
Then people I know are asking me,

00:32:29.740 --> 00:32:32.790
can you do this Geshe-la?
Can we have a meeting?

00:32:32.790 --> 00:32:34.480
Can we just talk for ten minutes?

00:32:34.480 --> 00:32:37.158
Can we go out and have coffee?

00:32:37.158 --> 00:32:40.340
Can you come over to my house?

00:32:40.340 --> 00:32:43.897
Someone told me recently they see,

00:32:44.953 --> 00:32:46.220
they live in Sedona they said,

00:32:46.220 --> 00:32:49.640
I see Stanley and Alison
more than I see you Geshe-la.

00:32:49.640 --> 00:32:50.870
They live in China.

00:32:53.180 --> 00:32:57.230
And I'm like, I'm sorry but it's intense,

00:32:57.230 --> 00:32:59.860
the amount of work is intense.

00:32:59.860 --> 00:33:02.200
And then the question is,

00:33:02.200 --> 00:33:04.480
is it a good spiritual practice

00:33:06.040 --> 00:33:09.410
to spend your whole day in books?

00:33:09.410 --> 00:33:12.120
It seems like Tsongkapa's thing

00:33:12.120 --> 00:33:17.120
that he was spending
most of his day in books

00:33:17.380 --> 00:33:20.840
and not really meeting a
lot of other people, and not

00:33:22.040 --> 00:33:27.040
socializing, and not getting
to see the people's real lives.

00:33:27.183 --> 00:33:28.870
It seems almost artificial

00:33:30.750 --> 00:33:32.580
to spend your whole day in books.

00:33:32.580 --> 00:33:33.880
And it also seems

00:33:35.270 --> 00:33:37.297
too technical.

00:33:37.297 --> 00:33:41.020
It seems, Geshe-la, like
if that's what it takes

00:33:41.020 --> 00:33:44.441
to meet Tsongkapa, if I have to read

00:33:44.441 --> 00:33:47.620
those thousands of pages
that the Mixed Nuts are

00:33:47.620 --> 00:33:52.410
spitting out, then it just
doesn't seem practical,

00:33:52.410 --> 00:33:55.230
it seems like it's too scholarly.

00:33:55.230 --> 00:33:59.910
So I wanted to say as a method

00:34:01.090 --> 00:34:04.510
of reaching those other
worlds, it's fantastic.

00:34:05.640 --> 00:34:09.710
I know it's not a popular thing to say

00:34:09.710 --> 00:34:12.090
and I know those books
are difficult books.

00:34:12.090 --> 00:34:15.520
They are difficult books. They
are really difficult books.

00:34:18.330 --> 00:34:21.870
But I want to say it's our lineage,

00:34:22.881 --> 00:34:24.990
in Tsongkapa's method,

00:34:28.490 --> 00:34:31.540
to put your head in those
books a couple hours

00:34:31.540 --> 00:34:36.120
a day and struggle. It's not easy.

00:34:36.120 --> 00:34:38.940
It's not easy. It's difficult

00:34:38.940 --> 00:34:43.650
and it's a hard. It's
just hard to sit there.

00:34:43.650 --> 00:34:46.190
It's hard to read

00:34:47.340 --> 00:34:49.130
hour after hour

00:34:49.130 --> 00:34:51.229
things that you don't understand.

00:34:51.229 --> 00:34:53.330
It's just frustrating,

00:34:53.330 --> 00:34:56.040
and I don't know,

00:34:56.040 --> 00:34:59.190
it's like trying to
read a foreign language

00:34:59.190 --> 00:35:01.940
and you can't get it.

00:35:01.940 --> 00:35:04.513
There's foreign languages
that you can't: French.

00:35:05.630 --> 00:35:08.220
I decided three times to learn French

00:35:08.220 --> 00:35:09.580
or Chinese,

00:35:12.356 --> 00:35:13.790
and it's frustrating.

00:35:13.790 --> 00:35:16.050
And it doesn't seem

00:35:16.050 --> 00:35:19.490
very mystical and it
doesn't seem very sweet.

00:35:19.490 --> 00:35:22.880
And rasa, it doesn't have much flavor.

00:35:25.360 --> 00:35:27.240
But I want to describe what happens

00:35:28.410 --> 00:35:30.250
and I think it happened to Tsongkapa

00:35:30.250 --> 00:35:32.363
if you read his life story.

00:35:34.230 --> 00:35:35.890
We are trying to invite

00:35:38.140 --> 00:35:41.460
with the practice of The Thousand Angels,

00:35:41.460 --> 00:35:46.460
we are trying to invite
to our meditation room

00:35:46.810 --> 00:35:51.810
a person who spent many, many years

00:35:54.620 --> 00:35:58.650
deep inside those ancient classics

00:35:58.650 --> 00:36:00.580
that John Brady has been saving,

00:36:01.800 --> 00:36:06.440
and because of that, he found a door,

00:36:06.440 --> 00:36:10.753
he created a door to meet these beings

00:36:12.680 --> 00:36:14.280
from another world.

00:36:14.280 --> 00:36:17.320
And Tibet as a country,

00:36:17.320 --> 00:36:18.760
as a, what do you call it?,

00:36:18.760 --> 00:36:21.350
governmental structure,

00:36:21.350 --> 00:36:22.713
it's lousy.

00:36:24.515 --> 00:36:27.863
I mean, it's like below average.

00:36:30.830 --> 00:36:34.200
I'm sorry, as a country,
it's kind of dysfunctional.

00:36:36.150 --> 00:36:40.610
That's it not the point of
what's going on in Tibet.

00:36:40.610 --> 00:36:45.610
The point is that there are people there

00:36:46.070 --> 00:36:48.683
who worked on these ideas,

00:36:50.050 --> 00:36:52.130
struggled through those great books,

00:36:53.240 --> 00:36:55.070
day after day,

00:36:55.070 --> 00:36:57.740
and the karma of that

00:36:57.740 --> 00:37:02.330
was that they opened a window
to another world, you see?

00:37:02.330 --> 00:37:06.730
People came from another world

00:37:06.730 --> 00:37:10.320
and help them, and we can do it too.

00:37:10.320 --> 00:37:14.883
So when you do the practice
of The Thousand Angels,

00:37:16.820 --> 00:37:21.310
what's really happening is
you are trying to open a door

00:37:22.424 --> 00:37:24.920
and then you will meet these

00:37:27.570 --> 00:37:31.470
unbelievable people from another realm.

00:37:31.470 --> 00:37:33.560
And they aren't,

00:37:33.560 --> 00:37:35.450
they're not like us

00:37:35.450 --> 00:37:38.450
and it's even uncomfortable
to be with them

00:37:38.450 --> 00:37:40.430
because they're so good it's frustrating.

00:37:41.470 --> 00:37:44.663
And you feel,

00:37:46.830 --> 00:37:49.443
you feel like an idiot when
you're sitting with them.

00:37:49.443 --> 00:37:54.443
So I really want to encourage you

00:37:56.477 --> 00:38:00.610
to learn this practice.

00:38:00.610 --> 00:38:04.543
I know it's very foreign.

00:38:05.690 --> 00:38:10.690
I know it's not a language
that we're familiar with.

00:38:11.350 --> 00:38:14.920
I know even the main guy's
name is hard to pronounce

00:38:17.630 --> 00:38:22.630
but without being romantic,
and what do you call it?,

00:38:23.230 --> 00:38:28.230
sentimental, you can open
a window to another world.

00:38:29.780 --> 00:38:33.400
And those Himalayas, they were,

00:38:33.400 --> 00:38:38.400
Shangri-La, they real a
doorway to another world.

00:38:39.500 --> 00:38:44.230
Again, I'm not attracted to Tibetan

00:38:45.360 --> 00:38:47.363
country as a country.

00:38:48.370 --> 00:38:49.910
It's just another country.

00:38:49.910 --> 00:38:53.520
It's not different from
any country you've been to.

00:38:55.160 --> 00:38:59.280
But the doorway is there.

00:38:59.280 --> 00:39:02.334
And if you practice The Thousand Angels,

00:39:02.334 --> 00:39:04.610
you can open that doorway.

00:39:04.610 --> 00:39:05.530
I'm not going to,

00:39:05.530 --> 00:39:07.960
I personally,

00:39:07.960 --> 00:39:11.390
I've taken you through those steps

00:39:11.390 --> 00:39:14.266
in The Thousand Angels many times.

00:39:14.266 --> 00:39:17.485
I kind of want to talk
about something else today.

00:39:17.485 --> 00:39:20.320
You can do those on your own

00:39:20.320 --> 00:39:22.870
and you don't need me to explain to you

00:39:22.870 --> 00:39:26.010
which flower is blue
and which flower is red,

00:39:26.010 --> 00:39:30.062
that you're going to be
offering. You can do that.

00:39:32.340 --> 00:39:34.510
But I'd like to talk about an experience.

00:39:34.510 --> 00:39:37.410
So I've been translating,

00:39:37.410 --> 00:39:40.090
I've been helping prepare

00:39:40.090 --> 00:39:42.493
a book by,

00:39:43.800 --> 00:39:47.940
it's being translated by
Venerable Utpala, Bets Greer.

00:39:47.940 --> 00:39:52.470
She's been working on this
book for about five years

00:39:52.470 --> 00:39:55.890
and many of you have
been through the classes.

00:39:55.890 --> 00:39:58.880
And it was hard.

00:39:58.880 --> 00:40:00.850
The book was hard.

00:40:00.850 --> 00:40:04.360
It's supposed to be

00:40:04.360 --> 00:40:07.440
a book of emptiness meditations.

00:40:07.440 --> 00:40:09.714
And we worked on it,

00:40:09.714 --> 00:40:12.710
many of you guys came to the classes,

00:40:12.710 --> 00:40:17.710
and we spend an hour,
we go about half a page.

00:40:18.590 --> 00:40:20.373
We can't understand much.

00:40:21.450 --> 00:40:24.550
I know the words, I can explain it to you.

00:40:24.550 --> 00:40:28.190
But it's difficult. It's
really, really difficult.

00:40:28.190 --> 00:40:32.159
And she finished, she finished her book.

00:40:32.159 --> 00:40:36.540
Then I have to kind of
work on the translation,

00:40:36.540 --> 00:40:37.970
make it smooth.

00:40:37.970 --> 00:40:42.390
Sp I have a pleasant

00:40:42.390 --> 00:40:45.120
duty that I have to go through

00:40:45.120 --> 00:40:48.490
and make the whole translation.

00:40:48.490 --> 00:40:51.720
I have to really

00:40:51.720 --> 00:40:54.510
connect the five years of classes

00:40:54.510 --> 00:40:59.390
into one beautiful flow and that's my job.

00:40:59.390 --> 00:41:01.620
So I started

00:41:01.620 --> 00:41:05.150
and then that starts blowing my mind.

00:41:05.150 --> 00:41:09.180
I start seeing this pattern:

00:41:09.180 --> 00:41:12.080
I taught the book to her for five years

00:41:12.080 --> 00:41:14.610
and I didn't see the pattern.

00:41:14.610 --> 00:41:16.630
Now I have to lay the whole thing out

00:41:16.630 --> 00:41:17.860
and I'm like, oh my god.

00:41:19.960 --> 00:41:23.000
It's 25 emptiness meditations

00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:25.880
and they're stunning.
They're just stunning.

00:41:27.030 --> 00:41:32.030
It's not one or two proofs of
emptiness, it's twenty five,

00:41:32.250 --> 00:41:37.250
one after another. They're
deep. They're very, very deep.

00:41:38.110 --> 00:41:41.423
And if you can't just,

00:41:42.620 --> 00:41:45.930
if you don't spend time
with them, you don't get it.

00:41:45.930 --> 00:41:47.980
One and Many: things are not one

00:41:49.010 --> 00:41:50.730
and things are not more than one.

00:41:50.730 --> 00:41:55.000
Things are not one and
things are not more than one.

00:41:55.000 --> 00:41:56.490
Really. Why?

00:41:56.490 --> 00:41:59.120
Because they have parts.

00:41:59.120 --> 00:42:00.700
Things are not one,

00:42:00.700 --> 00:42:04.050
nothing in the world is one thing

00:42:04.050 --> 00:42:06.400
and nothing in the world
is more than one thing

00:42:07.900 --> 00:42:10.280
because they have parts.
Everything has parts.

00:42:11.300 --> 00:42:13.410
And then they go on like that.

00:42:13.410 --> 00:42:15.610
It's a long, long,

00:42:15.610 --> 00:42:18.640
oh my god, twenty five proofs.

00:42:18.640 --> 00:42:21.930
And then there's another flow under it,

00:42:21.930 --> 00:42:25.420
which is through the great four schools.

00:42:25.420 --> 00:42:29.070
So sometimes you get the same argument

00:42:29.070 --> 00:42:31.530
taught from a different school.

00:42:31.530 --> 00:42:36.070
So he repeats the argument
of One and Many, three times,

00:42:36.070 --> 00:42:38.570
but from different schools.

00:42:38.570 --> 00:42:42.110
And then it's unbelievable.
It's just unbelievable

00:42:42.110 --> 00:42:46.322
and then suddenly you're
like, oh my gosh, I get it.

00:42:46.322 --> 00:42:49.100
I finally got it and then he says,

00:42:49.100 --> 00:42:51.030
wait, let me tell you something else.

00:42:51.030 --> 00:42:53.760
nd you're like, okay, I
got it, I got 25% emptiness

00:42:53.760 --> 00:42:56.030
in my head and I understand it.

00:42:56.030 --> 00:42:58.003
And I just used it with my wife.

00:42:59.920 --> 00:43:01.410
That's the cool thing, right?

00:43:01.410 --> 00:43:05.290
It's like, oh my god, I
got it in the morning,

00:43:05.290 --> 00:43:09.260
I translated it, and in
the afternoon I used it

00:43:09.260 --> 00:43:12.400
when she asked me why I didn't
do the laundry or something.

00:43:12.400 --> 00:43:16.542
I actually took one of
those proofs of emptiness

00:43:16.542 --> 00:43:20.470
and I secretly used it,

00:43:20.470 --> 00:43:24.450
and I opened a portal to
another world by using it,

00:43:24.450 --> 00:43:26.630
and I was, so wow.

00:43:26.630 --> 00:43:28.893
I was like, wow, that's cool.

00:43:30.510 --> 00:43:33.440
Oh, you have parts.
Your laundry has parts.

00:43:33.440 --> 00:43:35.562
And she's like, huh?

00:43:35.562 --> 00:43:40.562
I got it. Oh! You know, and then

00:43:40.876 --> 00:43:45.240
the author, who is called Chone Lama,

00:43:45.240 --> 00:43:46.220
he lived

00:43:48.630 --> 00:43:51.890
250 years after Tsongkapa,

00:43:51.890 --> 00:43:54.960
but I think he was Tsongkapa.

00:43:54.960 --> 00:43:57.282
I think he was Tsongkapa.

00:43:57.282 --> 00:43:59.030
A lot of the books

00:43:59.030 --> 00:44:01.370
we are transcending, Seiji knows,

00:44:01.370 --> 00:44:06.370
there are from Chone Lama,
and he's like Tsongkapa

00:44:06.400 --> 00:44:10.810
but more accessible and
he's more reachable.

00:44:10.810 --> 00:44:12.540
And so he says, hey,

00:44:12.540 --> 00:44:15.420
you liked the twenty five?
Worked with the laundry, huh?

00:44:15.420 --> 00:44:16.940
Like you get to know these guys,

00:44:16.940 --> 00:44:18.310
you're like,

00:44:18.310 --> 00:44:20.920
- -Hey it worked with the
laundry and your wife, right?

00:44:20.920 --> 00:44:23.440
I say, Yeah, yeah, it was,

00:44:23.440 --> 00:44:24.607
it didn't just work,

00:44:24.607 --> 00:44:28.230
it was like opening a
door to another world

00:44:28.230 --> 00:44:30.120
in the washroom.

00:44:31.142 --> 00:44:33.740
Then he's like, Well, let
me show you something else.

00:44:33.740 --> 00:44:36.643
Then he goes through fifteen proofs of,

00:44:38.270 --> 00:44:41.210
fifteen mistaken proofs of emptiness,

00:44:41.210 --> 00:44:46.210
slightly defective emptiness
proofs and that's so cool.

00:44:47.181 --> 00:44:49.630
He says, Hey, I got a proof for you,

00:44:49.630 --> 00:44:50.780
how about this one?

00:44:50.780 --> 00:44:52.640
And then you go, you
read it and then he says,

00:44:52.640 --> 00:44:54.090
- - How do you like that one?

00:44:54.090 --> 00:44:55.190
And you're like,

00:44:55.190 --> 00:44:56.650
- - Sounds great to me, and he says,

00:44:56.650 --> 00:44:58.760
- - Nah, it's messed up.

00:44:58.760 --> 00:45:00.550
And you're like, Why is it messed up?

00:45:00.550 --> 00:45:02.270
And he says, Well, look
at this little thing here,

00:45:02.270 --> 00:45:03.210
it doesn't work.

00:45:03.210 --> 00:45:05.190
And you're like, Yeah,
I never thought of that,

00:45:05.190 --> 00:45:07.350
that doesn't work does it?

00:45:07.350 --> 00:45:10.820
So after he teaches you twenty five,

00:45:10.820 --> 00:45:15.040
is it twenty three correct
proofs of emptiness,

00:45:15.040 --> 00:45:19.790
from all four and a half
schools of ancient Buddhism,

00:45:19.790 --> 00:45:23.170
then he says, hHy, let's
do some messed up proofs,

00:45:23.170 --> 00:45:25.150
let's go through some messed up proofs.

00:45:25.150 --> 00:45:28.260
I'll mess something up and
you tell me what's messed up.

00:45:28.260 --> 00:45:30.230
And then you're like, I
don't see anything messed up

00:45:30.230 --> 00:45:34.680
and then he takes you through fifteen

00:45:34.680 --> 00:45:36.520
different messed up proofs to emptiness

00:45:36.520 --> 00:45:39.560
that you've probably said
to your friends many times.

00:45:39.560 --> 00:45:43.360
It's just awesome.

00:45:43.360 --> 00:45:45.740
Then you're like, Oh man I'm so happy

00:45:45.740 --> 00:45:47.270
and I'm almost at the end of the book,

00:45:47.270 --> 00:45:51.743
and I can send it off
Elly to get it printed.

00:45:53.550 --> 00:45:55.520
Everyone's going to be so happy.

00:45:55.520 --> 00:45:57.896
And then he, at the end
of the book, he says,

00:45:57.896 --> 00:46:01.280
I forgot to tell you how to
meditate on the emptiness.

00:46:01.280 --> 00:46:05.794
And you're like, How he going
to do that with 2 pages left?

00:46:05.794 --> 00:46:07.250
How's he going to teach you

00:46:07.250 --> 00:46:10.098
how to meditate with two pages left?

00:46:10.098 --> 00:46:11.893
And then he says, Well,

00:46:13.160 --> 00:46:15.430
I don't really have space

00:46:15.430 --> 00:46:18.700
in the book anymore to tell
you how to meditate on it.

00:46:18.700 --> 00:46:21.303
I'll tell you there's three
steps to the meditation.

00:46:22.500 --> 00:46:25.323
First you have to learn the book.

00:46:26.720 --> 00:46:30.450
You must get a hold of an emptiness book

00:46:30.450 --> 00:46:32.660
and you must spend time

00:46:32.660 --> 00:46:35.350
with a qualified teacher and read it.

00:46:35.350 --> 00:46:37.570
And you have to

00:46:37.570 --> 00:46:42.300
struggle with those ideas.
You have to struggle.

00:46:42.300 --> 00:46:44.340
Learn the correct ones.

00:46:44.340 --> 00:46:46.100
Learn the wrong ones.

00:46:46.100 --> 00:46:48.760
Struggle why this is
correct, this is wrong.

00:46:48.760 --> 00:46:50.620
Struggle with why

00:46:50.620 --> 00:46:53.220
this school explains
the same proof different

00:46:53.220 --> 00:46:54.900
from that school.

00:46:54.900 --> 00:46:56.433
Struggle with those things.

00:46:57.540 --> 00:47:00.323
That's called Sruthi, right?

00:47:03.010 --> 00:47:05.573
Learning in the class, classroom hours.

00:47:06.770 --> 00:47:09.410
And then I wanted to go to BSAM PA, right?

00:47:09.410 --> 00:47:11.087
What is that?

00:47:11.087 --> 00:47:13.580
%Cintaya or something.

00:47:13.580 --> 00:47:17.010
I want you to contemplate
what you learned.

00:47:17.010 --> 00:47:19.310
For me, that's when I'm driving.

00:47:19.310 --> 00:47:20.700
I don't know, when driving,

00:47:20.700 --> 00:47:22.150
Veronica swears by it.

00:47:22.150 --> 00:47:24.960
She says driving is my meditation time.

00:47:24.960 --> 00:47:26.430
It's actually a contemplation time.

00:47:26.430 --> 00:47:28.660
If you meditate, you'll crash.

00:47:28.660 --> 00:47:32.410
So she's like, she mulls things over

00:47:32.410 --> 00:47:35.070
and she thinks things over in the car,

00:47:35.070 --> 00:47:38.875
and it's a really sweet practice.

00:47:38.875 --> 00:47:41.130
So you're like, well,

00:47:41.130 --> 00:47:44.790
so I'm having trouble
with this jewelry thing.

00:47:44.790 --> 00:47:48.080
Let's see, does it have parts?

00:47:48.080 --> 00:47:53.080
Is it empty? And you do that in the car

00:47:53.598 --> 00:47:57.073
and then you get to
that and, then he says,

00:47:58.660 --> 00:48:00.153
then you can get to,

00:48:02.140 --> 00:48:06.190
then you can meditate on
what you contemplated on

00:48:06.190 --> 00:48:08.600
when you get home in the car,

00:48:08.600 --> 00:48:10.260
then get out of the car

00:48:10.260 --> 00:48:13.470
and take 20 minutes on your cushion,

00:48:13.470 --> 00:48:16.890
and go into it deep and see if
you can see it in meditation,

00:48:16.890 --> 00:48:20.650
what you learned in the car
that you learned from the book.

00:48:20.650 --> 00:48:24.750
Then he stops the book.
Chone Lama stops the book.

00:48:24.750 --> 00:48:27.060
So I was frustrated and I said,

00:48:27.060 --> 00:48:29.010
This is kind of dumb.

00:48:29.010 --> 00:48:32.480
We're going to call this
book, emptiness meditations

00:48:32.480 --> 00:48:34.870
and there's 38 proofs of emptiness

00:48:34.870 --> 00:48:38.980
and there's three
sentences about meditation?

00:48:38.980 --> 00:48:43.520
Then, you know, that's
not going to go over well.

00:48:44.628 --> 00:48:49.570
Let's add the meditation
section from Pabongka Rinpoche

00:48:49.570 --> 00:48:52.250
to the second half of the book.

00:48:52.250 --> 00:48:55.000
Let's add it to the book so then you get

00:48:56.760 --> 00:48:59.680
in the first half of the
book, like 200 pages,

00:48:59.680 --> 00:49:01.530
you get emptiness proofs,

00:49:01.530 --> 00:49:03.883
and then you get 200
pages of how to meditate,

00:49:05.720 --> 00:49:08.090
all the details of how to meditate.

00:49:08.090 --> 00:49:09.160
And I said, oh wow,

00:49:09.160 --> 00:49:11.717
that's what we'll do.

00:49:11.717 --> 00:49:16.090
We'll add Pabongka Rinpoche's
explanation cause it's really,

00:49:16.090 --> 00:49:17.950
it's also,

00:49:17.950 --> 00:49:19.570
I've taught it so many times

00:49:19.570 --> 00:49:22.420
that I could translate
with my eyes closed.

00:49:22.420 --> 00:49:24.800
And I said, Ah, just knock that out.

00:49:24.800 --> 00:49:26.073
And so,

00:49:28.030 --> 00:49:30.220
that's going to be 200 more pages.

00:49:30.220 --> 00:49:32.737
And then I thought, well,

00:49:32.737 --> 00:49:36.390
he based his meditation

00:49:36.390 --> 00:49:38.600
description on

00:49:40.286 --> 00:49:42.060
on Kamalashila's

00:49:42.060 --> 00:49:46.530
Stages of Meditation and
there's a beautiful chart,

00:49:46.530 --> 00:49:48.710
there's a beautiful carving

00:49:48.710 --> 00:49:50.810
of all the stages of meditation.

00:49:50.810 --> 00:49:55.340
They kept it in the...I
shouldn't say it....

00:49:55.340 --> 00:49:58.330
Anyway, I ran into this chart once

00:49:58.330 --> 00:50:03.190
and I copied it. I mean,
I took photographs of it

00:50:03.190 --> 00:50:05.740
and I learned what it
meant. I translated it.

00:50:05.740 --> 00:50:07.510
I learned to read it.

00:50:07.510 --> 00:50:10.330
And so I said, well, let's
put the chart in the book

00:50:10.330 --> 00:50:12.660
and that will be beautiful for people,

00:50:12.660 --> 00:50:14.460
and I'll translate the whole chart.

00:50:14.460 --> 00:50:17.640
So we did, we got the whole chart

00:50:17.640 --> 00:50:20.240
and we put it in the book.

00:50:20.240 --> 00:50:24.720
And then I was like, Well, this chart

00:50:24.720 --> 00:50:26.750
comes from Kamalashila

00:50:27.960 --> 00:50:31.090
and it's interesting cause he's an Indian

00:50:31.090 --> 00:50:33.300
who was a great meditator

00:50:33.300 --> 00:50:36.090
and a great emptiness master,

00:50:36.090 --> 00:50:38.610
and a great Mind-Only master.

00:50:38.610 --> 00:50:43.610
You guys read his commentary,

00:50:44.020 --> 00:50:46.470
we went through his commentary
on the Diamond Cutter Sutra.

00:50:48.607 --> 00:50:49.940
He actually went to Tibet

00:50:49.940 --> 00:50:52.750
and he had some interesting
debates with people

00:50:52.750 --> 00:50:55.040
and stuff like that. So he was passionate

00:50:56.450 --> 00:50:59.290
about teaching people meditation.

00:50:59.290 --> 00:51:04.150
Then he wrote three famous books

00:51:04.150 --> 00:51:06.310
as John knows, he went
and got them for me,

00:51:07.632 --> 00:51:10.130
called "The Stages of Meditation".

00:51:10.130 --> 00:51:13.850
They kind of overlap. You can tell

00:51:13.850 --> 00:51:17.299
they might be manuals
that he prepared for DCI,

00:51:17.299 --> 00:51:18.960
SCIM, and ACI.

00:51:18.960 --> 00:51:21.873
And so it's the same stuff
in a different package.

00:51:21.873 --> 00:51:25.180
Then there's a fourth one,

00:51:25.180 --> 00:51:28.500
a very beautiful one that he wrote.

00:51:28.500 --> 00:51:30.990
So I was looking at those

00:51:30.990 --> 00:51:33.560
and I was trying to choose
which one to translate.

00:51:33.560 --> 00:51:37.660
Then I noticed there's another
stages of the meditation

00:51:38.730 --> 00:51:42.760
in the Tengyur from ancient India.

00:51:42.760 --> 00:51:46.243
This is, I said, oh, I
wonder who wrote that?

00:51:46.243 --> 00:51:48.418
Nagarjuna.

00:51:48.418 --> 00:51:51.300
Arya Nagarjuna I said, Oh my god,

00:51:51.300 --> 00:51:55.090
there's another book on how to meditate,

00:51:55.090 --> 00:51:59.070
written by the greatest
emptiness master of all time?

00:51:59.070 --> 00:52:01.250
Wow, let's go look at that.

00:52:02.625 --> 00:52:07.625
It's got the same name as
Kamalashila's three books.

00:52:07.700 --> 00:52:09.100
It's the same name.

00:52:09.100 --> 00:52:09.933
So I'm like, Wow,

00:52:09.933 --> 00:52:11.410
I wonder if Kamalashila ripped this off

00:52:11.410 --> 00:52:12.870
from Nagarjuna,

00:52:12.870 --> 00:52:16.440
and the way I'm ripping the
mine off of Kamalashila,

00:52:16.440 --> 00:52:19.017
and the way Pabonka and me ripped off it.

00:52:20.776 --> 00:52:22.750
So I went and read that one

00:52:22.750 --> 00:52:27.340
and it's a stunning book about
the stages of meditation,

00:52:27.340 --> 00:52:30.143
heavily mixed with emptiness teachings,

00:52:31.250 --> 00:52:35.343
heavy, heavy emptiness
teachings and how to meditate.

00:52:35.343 --> 00:52:38.190
So you got this thing, you see,

00:52:38.190 --> 00:52:43.190
you could learn the posture of retreat,

00:52:43.380 --> 00:52:45.550
learn everything about how to meditate

00:52:45.550 --> 00:52:47.630
from Pabongka Rinpoche

00:52:47.630 --> 00:52:49.553
Then use the chart.

00:52:50.650 --> 00:52:53.160
Put the chart in your meditation room,

00:52:53.160 --> 00:52:57.720
and use that every day to
work on your meditation.

00:52:57.720 --> 00:53:02.720
And then go through
Kamalashila's meditation book

00:53:04.760 --> 00:53:09.760
and then go through Nagarjuna's
book, with the same name,

00:53:10.610 --> 00:53:12.660
but deeper on the emptiness part,

00:53:12.660 --> 00:53:17.660
and then slide into Chone
Lama's 38 proofs the emptiness,

00:53:18.240 --> 00:53:20.853
which is really just Tsongkapa recooked.

00:53:22.150 --> 00:53:22.983
You see what I mean?

00:53:22.983 --> 00:53:27.430
So you get this whole
picture of a huge work:

00:53:27.430 --> 00:53:30.940
half vipashayana, half shamatha,

00:53:30.940 --> 00:53:33.930
first half how to see emptiness,

00:53:33.930 --> 00:53:38.020
second half how to get into
meditation to see emptiness.

00:53:38.020 --> 00:53:40.980
So now you've got 200 pages

00:53:40.980 --> 00:53:44.060
on vipashayana, how to see emptiness,

00:53:44.060 --> 00:53:48.263
and then you got 200 pages
on how to meditate, shamatha.

00:53:49.460 --> 00:53:54.460
So really it's this now, poor Bets' book,

00:53:54.740 --> 00:53:58.060
has become this great, incredible

00:54:00.200 --> 00:54:03.710
book. It's a real
emptiness meditation book.

00:54:03.710 --> 00:54:08.710
So half of it is how
to understand emptiness

00:54:09.070 --> 00:54:12.023
and then half of it is how to meditate,

00:54:13.050 --> 00:54:15.450
which is the great marriage

00:54:15.450 --> 00:54:17.644
of vipashayana and shamatha.

00:54:17.644 --> 00:54:20.147
Vipashayana: insight into emptiness

00:54:20.147 --> 00:54:24.760
Shamatha: quiet, quietude,
getting silent, silence.

00:54:24.760 --> 00:54:29.760
Silence and insight matched
together in one book.

00:54:31.060 --> 00:54:33.768
Guess who did that before?

00:54:35.140 --> 00:54:36.930
Tsongkapa's in a retreat

00:54:36.930 --> 00:54:41.490
and he's like, God, we should make a book

00:54:41.490 --> 00:54:44.123
that's 50% vipashayana and 50% shamatha.

00:54:46.860 --> 00:54:49.030
And he writes like,

00:54:49.030 --> 00:54:51.280
it would be about a
thousand pages in English

00:54:52.494 --> 00:54:54.460
and he just knocks it out.

00:54:54.460 --> 00:54:56.690
And then, I don't know, Manjrushi is like,

00:54:56.690 --> 00:55:00.400
Hey why don't you do the
first four perfections,

00:55:00.400 --> 00:55:01.393
throw it in there.

00:55:02.410 --> 00:55:03.707
Let's call it Lam Rim.

00:55:05.130 --> 00:55:09.250
So he's got emptiness teaching,

00:55:09.250 --> 00:55:12.830
shamatha, joined together
and then Manjrushi says,

00:55:12.830 --> 00:55:16.160
Ah, tack on this Lam Rim
stuff at the beginning.

00:55:16.160 --> 00:55:18.423
And so,

00:55:21.409 --> 00:55:22.680
that's what Tsongkapa did,

00:55:22.680 --> 00:55:24.610
So that's what Tsongkapa was up to.

00:55:24.610 --> 00:55:27.108
Why am I talking about that?

00:55:28.390 --> 00:55:30.713
Well, first of all, I'm
obsessed with it nowadays.

00:55:32.120 --> 00:55:33.503
But secondly,

00:55:34.830 --> 00:55:39.570
use it when you do your
Thousand Angels practice.

00:55:39.570 --> 00:55:42.140
Try to understand

00:55:42.140 --> 00:55:44.490
that you are going to be doing,

00:55:44.490 --> 00:55:46.722
let's go through it okay?

00:55:46.722 --> 00:55:49.038
PHYAG 'TSAL BA DANG

00:55:49.038 --> 00:55:51.821
MCHOD CING BSHAGS PA DANG

00:55:51.821 --> 00:55:53.040
RJES SU YI RANG

00:55:53.040 --> 00:55:55.690
These are the seven steps, right?

00:55:55.690 --> 00:55:58.500
First one, PHYAG 'TSAL BA

00:55:58.500 --> 00:56:02.213
Bow down to...How much time I got left?

00:56:03.630 --> 00:56:05.890
Okay, yeah, we got time.

00:56:05.890 --> 00:56:09.250
So the basic structure

00:56:09.250 --> 00:56:11.610
of The Thousand Angels practice,

00:56:11.610 --> 00:56:15.820
which I would like it to
do with a special mantra,

00:56:15.820 --> 00:56:17.830
called OM MANI PADME HUNG,

00:56:17.830 --> 00:56:19.480
and I'll explain more about that.

00:56:21.190 --> 00:56:25.760
First thing, how to get this guy

00:56:25.760 --> 00:56:29.933
to come through the doorway
from the other realm.

00:56:31.520 --> 00:56:34.307
There's a certain etiquette.

00:56:34.307 --> 00:56:38.320
In the New Testament, the Bible,

00:56:38.320 --> 00:56:42.780
Jesus always washes his
disciples feet when they show up,

00:56:42.780 --> 00:56:46.550
which is very unusual for the master

00:56:46.550 --> 00:56:49.620
and we kind of got to do the same thing.

00:56:49.620 --> 00:56:54.030
It's like cookies for
Santa Claus under the tree.

00:56:54.030 --> 00:56:57.630
I don't know about you, but my
family was very serious about

00:56:57.630 --> 00:57:00.410
Christmas cookies for Santa Claus.

00:57:00.410 --> 00:57:02.627
One night I went out to see Santa Claus

00:57:02.627 --> 00:57:06.140
and I saw my dad eating them.

00:57:06.140 --> 00:57:07.313
But anyway,

00:57:09.750 --> 00:57:13.540
first thing, prostrate to Tsongkapa.

00:57:13.540 --> 00:57:16.390
Now I feel uncomfortable prostrating.

00:57:16.390 --> 00:57:17.980
I did grow up Christian

00:57:17.980 --> 00:57:19.560
and one of the rules in Christianity

00:57:19.560 --> 00:57:23.330
is not to bow down to, I don't know,

00:57:23.330 --> 00:57:25.302
unapproved objects.

00:57:25.302 --> 00:57:29.870
So I always felt uncomfortable
to do prostration

00:57:29.870 --> 00:57:34.870
but really the first step of
the DGA' LDAN LHA BRGYA MA

00:57:35.250 --> 00:57:40.250
is just to admire Tsongkapa
and that's a prostration

00:57:41.260 --> 00:57:42.440
and that's all.

00:57:42.440 --> 00:57:46.600
If you want to get some
exercise, then prostrate.

00:57:46.600 --> 00:57:48.740
But the real prostration

00:57:48.740 --> 00:57:50.743
is just to admire this guy.

00:57:53.120 --> 00:57:56.700
The real way to get him
to come through the portal

00:57:56.700 --> 00:58:00.562
and show up in your meditation
room, which is possible,

00:58:00.562 --> 00:58:02.110
that's what I'm trying to say today.

00:58:02.110 --> 00:58:04.800
It is possible, you can get him there,

00:58:04.800 --> 00:58:05.763
and it's awesome.

00:58:07.380 --> 00:58:10.070
First thing you have to
say, "god, you're so cool."

00:58:10.070 --> 00:58:11.980
You're just so cool.

00:58:11.980 --> 00:58:14.743
All the stuff you did,

00:58:16.950 --> 00:58:20.780
mainly that you taught us emptiness

00:58:20.780 --> 00:58:22.926
and how to meditate.

00:58:22.926 --> 00:58:27.510
You brought that into this
world from your world,

00:58:27.510 --> 00:58:28.870
that was cool.

00:58:28.870 --> 00:58:30.327
So if you just admire him,

00:58:30.327 --> 00:58:31.775
you did the first one.

00:58:31.775 --> 00:58:33.576
PHYAG 'TSAL BA DANG

00:58:33.576 --> 00:58:35.190
MCHOD means MCHOD PA,

00:58:35.190 --> 00:58:37.483
Yeah make some kind of offerings.

00:58:39.340 --> 00:58:42.200
I know it's a tradition
to offer water cups,

00:58:42.200 --> 00:58:46.530
and fruit, and stuff like that.

00:58:46.530 --> 00:58:48.700
I was never much into it. I'll be honest.

00:58:49.890 --> 00:58:51.030
I did it.

00:58:51.030 --> 00:58:53.703
I can make a TGOR MA as good as anybody.

00:58:57.216 --> 00:58:59.020
But what Tsongkapa really wants from you

00:58:59.020 --> 00:59:04.020
is an offering of your goodness.

00:59:04.350 --> 00:59:09.350
So he wants to hear that you
called somebody in the hospital

00:59:09.700 --> 00:59:13.020
or that you wash the dishes

00:59:14.800 --> 00:59:19.510
at the building after everybody else left,

00:59:19.510 --> 00:59:20.900
right Nour?

00:59:20.900 --> 00:59:25.823
The other roaches were running around.

00:59:30.140 --> 00:59:33.772
That's the kind of offering
that Tsongkapa really wants.

00:59:33.772 --> 00:59:36.100
My neighbor was pissing me off

00:59:36.100 --> 00:59:37.310
and I went out and talked to him,

00:59:37.310 --> 00:59:39.940
and asked him about his family,

00:59:39.940 --> 00:59:44.940
and I admired his new truck
with the decals on the back.

00:59:46.490 --> 00:59:50.957
And you know, that's a
great truck. I did it, okay?

00:59:52.910 --> 00:59:54.090
And that's the kind of thing.

00:59:54.090 --> 00:59:56.940
That's the offering Tsongkapa wants.

00:59:56.940 --> 00:59:58.370
It's okay if you're meditating

00:59:58.370 --> 01:00:00.980
and you're in a three day retreat.

01:00:00.980 --> 01:00:05.103
Okay, get some fruits,
and donuts, and stuff,

01:00:07.840 --> 01:00:10.520
and make offerings.
That's fine. That's good.

01:00:10.520 --> 01:00:14.780
My teacher would spend two or three hours

01:00:14.780 --> 01:00:19.190
at the grocery store checking
every kind of cookie,

01:00:19.190 --> 01:00:21.130
the whole aisle,

01:00:21.130 --> 01:00:22.470
every kind of cookie,

01:00:22.470 --> 01:00:26.320
and then he would decide on one

01:00:26.320 --> 01:00:30.620
and then he would carefully
stand there for half an hour

01:00:30.620 --> 01:00:32.270
and look through the plastic

01:00:32.270 --> 01:00:34.650
and try to see if any of them were chipped

01:00:34.650 --> 01:00:37.010
because it's improper to
offer a chipped cookie

01:00:37.010 --> 01:00:38.687
to Tsongkapa.

01:00:38.687 --> 01:00:42.550
So they should be perfect, that's fine.

01:00:42.550 --> 01:00:45.700
But also don't forget that what Tsongkapa

01:00:45.700 --> 01:00:50.620
really likes for offerings is some small,

01:00:50.620 --> 01:00:53.030
saying you did like wash the dishes

01:00:53.030 --> 01:00:55.450
at the college building

01:00:55.450 --> 01:00:57.570
after everybody else dumped them on you

01:00:58.760 --> 01:01:00.420
and went home,

01:01:00.420 --> 01:01:01.610
and you're trying to hold a baby

01:01:01.610 --> 01:01:02.650
and wash them with one hand.

01:01:02.650 --> 01:01:06.058
It's like, that's good yoga.

01:01:06.058 --> 01:01:08.993
You don't have to have barbells.

01:01:10.866 --> 01:01:13.130
PHYAG 'TSAL BA DANG MCHOD CING BSHAGS PA

01:01:13.130 --> 01:01:18.130
Then confess mistakes you've made.

01:01:18.160 --> 01:01:20.980
If you think you haven't
made any mistakes,

01:01:20.980 --> 01:01:23.750
that proves you're not meditating

01:01:23.750 --> 01:01:27.760
because you make mistakes all day

01:01:29.401 --> 01:01:32.220
and you repeat mistakes your whole life.

01:01:32.220 --> 01:01:34.670
I'm 60 something years old

01:01:34.670 --> 01:01:36.970
and I can tell you, 68,

01:01:36.970 --> 01:01:39.380
you repeat the same mistakes every year,

01:01:39.380 --> 01:01:41.160
over and over again.

01:01:41.160 --> 01:01:45.070
If you can't think of any
mistakes to tell Tsongkapa

01:01:45.070 --> 01:01:50.070
then you've reached the
real mindless meditation.

01:01:51.970 --> 01:01:55.680
So, tell the stuff you've done

01:01:55.680 --> 01:01:58.133
that you're not proud
of and get it out away.

01:02:00.010 --> 01:02:02.850
He enjoys talking to people

01:02:02.850 --> 01:02:05.630
who will admit that they made mistakes.

01:02:05.630 --> 01:02:07.310
If you're the kind of person

01:02:07.310 --> 01:02:09.830
who wants to pretend,
you're perfect, okay.

01:02:09.830 --> 01:02:13.110
But when you die, it's going to be messy.

01:02:13.110 --> 01:02:17.210
So just be honest about who you really are

01:02:17.210 --> 01:02:20.290
and tell Tsongkapa all your mistakes.

01:02:20.290 --> 01:02:22.840
Normally we tell everybody
our second worst mistake

01:02:22.840 --> 01:02:25.682
and we hide our first worst mistake,

01:02:25.682 --> 01:02:29.063
but with Tsongkapa, you can
tell them the worst one.

01:02:29.063 --> 01:02:31.004
PHYAG 'TSAL BA DANG
MCHOD CING BSHAGS PA DANG

01:02:31.004 --> 01:02:31.962
RJES SU YI RANG

01:02:31.962 --> 01:02:35.777
What's that? YI RANG

01:02:37.460 --> 01:02:39.280
Rejoice, be happy about other...

01:02:39.280 --> 01:02:41.991
There's so much good in the world.

01:02:44.964 --> 01:02:47.560
There are news outlets that talk about

01:02:47.560 --> 01:02:49.140
the great things people do.

01:02:49.140 --> 01:02:51.640
You got to work hard to find them.

01:02:51.640 --> 01:02:53.470
They're not very well known.

01:02:53.470 --> 01:02:56.100
They're not very popular

01:02:56.100 --> 01:03:00.170
but there are news
channels on the internet

01:03:00.170 --> 01:03:02.620
that honestly report,

01:03:03.810 --> 01:03:05.940
not grand good deeds by people

01:03:05.940 --> 01:03:07.710
but just normal people

01:03:07.710 --> 01:03:10.420
who are cooking food for homeless people,

01:03:10.420 --> 01:03:13.310
or doing nice things for people

01:03:13.310 --> 01:03:17.780
and you got to work
hard to find these news.

01:03:17.780 --> 01:03:21.210
The big news outlets are
only interested in scandals,

01:03:21.210 --> 01:03:26.210
and troubles, and wars
and it's very unbalanced.

01:03:28.030 --> 01:03:33.030
There's millions of people
doing kind things the whole day.

01:03:33.210 --> 01:03:34.463
So enjoy.

01:03:36.710 --> 01:03:38.700
Find one of those news outlets.

01:03:38.700 --> 01:03:42.870
I get this stupid magazine
from my university

01:03:42.870 --> 01:03:47.470
where they brag about all the
students and the professors.

01:03:47.470 --> 01:03:49.960
And it's so nice to read.

01:03:49.960 --> 01:03:53.111
Oh, this one just found out

01:03:53.111 --> 01:03:55.800
how the virus grows this bump on it,

01:03:55.800 --> 01:03:56.960
and how to take it off,

01:03:56.960 --> 01:04:01.380
and stop the virus. And this guy just,

01:04:01.380 --> 01:04:05.200
this secretary, who's been in
the McLean house at Princeton

01:04:05.200 --> 01:04:08.640
for 34 years just passed away,

01:04:08.640 --> 01:04:12.470
and she made coffee for
people every single day.

01:04:12.470 --> 01:04:17.460
And these nice little things,
so rejoice in the things

01:04:17.460 --> 01:04:19.232
that other people are doing.

01:04:19.232 --> 01:04:20.907
RJES SU YI RANG

01:04:20.907 --> 01:04:21.798
Then?

01:04:21.798 --> 01:04:22.906
BSKUL ZHING

01:04:25.250 --> 01:04:26.400
That's later.

01:04:26.400 --> 01:04:29.340
What happens after that?

01:04:29.340 --> 01:04:30.173
Request?

01:04:31.270 --> 01:04:32.820
Yeah ask him to teach.

01:04:32.820 --> 01:04:35.300
Ask him to teach you.

01:04:35.300 --> 01:04:38.260
And it doesn't mean

01:04:38.260 --> 01:04:40.140
Tsongkapa is going to
pop through his portal

01:04:40.140 --> 01:04:42.969
and start talking to you.

01:04:42.969 --> 01:04:46.713
He's probably going to send
you have a Mixed Nuts book

01:04:46.713 --> 01:04:49.410
and say, I hope you open it.

01:04:49.410 --> 01:04:54.410
I've been teaching a lot online.

01:04:55.510 --> 01:04:59.100
I've been teaching some deep, deep books

01:04:59.100 --> 01:05:02.960
and I have some students who prefer that,

01:05:02.960 --> 01:05:06.010
and they are very brave
and they are unusual.

01:05:06.010 --> 01:05:10.270
And I say, can I teach you
something that's not easy

01:05:10.270 --> 01:05:12.590
and that you probably won't understand?

01:05:12.590 --> 01:05:15.770
And they're like, "Yeah,
go ahead, Geshe-la".

01:05:15.770 --> 01:05:20.770
And then I'm like, "Listen,
when you study things,

01:05:21.050 --> 01:05:25.290
"when you try to read
things you can't understand,

01:05:25.290 --> 01:05:29.690
"that affects you more
than listening to things

01:05:29.690 --> 01:05:31.853
"that are comfortable for you."

01:05:33.950 --> 01:05:36.840
Things that are uncomfortable to hear

01:05:36.840 --> 01:05:39.190
because you don't understand them

01:05:39.190 --> 01:05:42.180
have a very powerful effect on your mind.

01:05:42.180 --> 01:05:45.460
Then things you know and
things you're familiar with,

01:05:45.460 --> 01:05:49.443
to hear them again, is not very helpful.

01:05:49.443 --> 01:05:53.880
So I have a small group of students,

01:05:53.880 --> 01:05:56.660
I'll say, can I just teach you something

01:05:56.660 --> 01:05:59.430
that you're not going to
understand for three years?

01:05:59.430 --> 01:06:01.290
And they're like, yeah, go ahead Geshe-la.

01:06:01.290 --> 01:06:05.450
They really work hard and
they don't understand it.

01:06:05.450 --> 01:06:08.900
But they try and when you try,

01:06:08.900 --> 01:06:11.450
it changes your brain.

01:06:11.450 --> 01:06:13.340
It changes the

01:06:13.340 --> 01:06:16.800
intelligence of you, spiritual
intelligence, it changes it.

01:06:16.800 --> 01:06:19.710
But just keep doing the same
thing you always heard of,

01:06:19.710 --> 01:06:21.150
that doesn't change much.

01:06:21.150 --> 01:06:25.140
So struggling mentally with new ideas

01:06:27.060 --> 01:06:28.610
is extremely

01:06:31.710 --> 01:06:33.360
powerful on your mind.

01:06:33.360 --> 01:06:34.930
Okay, I'm just saying,

01:06:34.930 --> 01:06:37.510
try it for six months or so.

01:06:37.510 --> 01:06:40.500
Read stuff you have no idea what it means

01:06:40.500 --> 01:06:42.870
and just struggle, struggle, struggle.

01:06:42.870 --> 01:06:47.870
And that's going to
change your entire being

01:06:48.600 --> 01:06:50.350
much more than reading something

01:06:50.350 --> 01:06:53.380
that you already familiar with.

01:06:53.380 --> 01:06:56.340
So anyway, you're asking for teaching.

01:06:56.340 --> 01:06:59.790
Don't forget the most powerful

01:06:59.790 --> 01:07:02.920
thing when you ask for
teaching, they might send

01:07:06.280 --> 01:07:09.240
trouble people who teach you stuff.

01:07:09.240 --> 01:07:12.070
People who hurt you teach you more

01:07:12.070 --> 01:07:14.080
than people who help you.

01:07:14.080 --> 01:07:15.720
I'm sorry, that's the way it is.

01:07:15.720 --> 01:07:20.720
So, when you ask for teaching,
watch out what you ask for

01:07:21.520 --> 01:07:23.053
because you might get a whole pile of

01:07:23.053 --> 01:07:26.040
irritating people showing up.

01:07:26.040 --> 01:07:28.342
And that's a blessing.

01:07:28.342 --> 01:07:33.342
I know you don't believe it but it's true.

01:07:33.770 --> 01:07:38.770
When you have to struggle with somebody,

01:07:38.970 --> 01:07:42.020
you advance. You become more advanced.

01:07:42.020 --> 01:07:45.368
If you're just comfortable
with people you know,

01:07:45.368 --> 01:07:48.130
you don't change much.

01:07:48.130 --> 01:07:50.776
All right, what's the next one?

01:07:51.640 --> 01:07:54.095
Yeah, ask them to stay.

01:07:54.095 --> 01:07:56.633
And I have people all the time,

01:07:58.916 --> 01:08:01.170
it's, "oh please stay."

01:08:01.170 --> 01:08:04.527
And I'm like, yeah, I hope I can.

01:08:05.558 --> 01:08:08.883
And I also would like to stay.

01:08:10.550 --> 01:08:14.715
But it's a terrible tragedy

01:08:14.715 --> 01:08:18.276
to come close to wisdom and lose it.

01:08:18.276 --> 01:08:21.526
That's a real tragedy to come close to,

01:08:24.756 --> 01:08:29.745
to come close to being
able to do a great retreat

01:08:31.407 --> 01:08:33.930
and then lose it is a terrible,

01:08:33.930 --> 01:08:37.484
I don't think there's anything
more tragic than that.

01:08:37.484 --> 01:08:41.850
I talked to this famous movie maker

01:08:41.850 --> 01:08:44.260
who has been writing,
he's been emailing me.

01:08:44.260 --> 01:08:46.700
I never met him

01:08:46.700 --> 01:08:48.460
in person. I never met him in person

01:08:48.460 --> 01:08:50.730
and he just got cancer.

01:08:50.730 --> 01:08:54.960
And he said, well,
okay, I'll do the chemo.

01:08:54.960 --> 01:08:58.140
And they said, don't bother.

01:08:58.140 --> 01:08:59.490
And he's like, what?

01:08:59.490 --> 01:09:00.457
Can I do anything?

01:09:00.457 --> 01:09:02.620
And they said, go home and die.

01:09:02.620 --> 01:09:05.640
Don't take up space in the hospital.

01:09:05.640 --> 01:09:08.140
Your wife can keep you as
comfortable as possible.

01:09:08.140 --> 01:09:11.170
Here's Brompton's cocktail,
you know what this is?

01:09:11.170 --> 01:09:13.814
It's what do you call that stuff?

01:09:13.814 --> 01:09:15.072
(indistinct chatter)

01:09:15.072 --> 01:09:16.740
It's like heroin.

01:09:16.740 --> 01:09:18.460
It's like straight heroin.

01:09:18.460 --> 01:09:20.300
They said here, when it gets bad,

01:09:20.300 --> 01:09:23.102
when it gets into your bones, take this.

01:09:23.102 --> 01:09:26.340
And then you'll die.

01:09:26.340 --> 01:09:27.890
Say anything you want
to say to your family

01:09:27.890 --> 01:09:29.810
because you won't be
able to talk after that.

01:09:29.810 --> 01:09:33.130
You'll just be a vegetable,
but at least you'll be alive.

01:09:33.130 --> 01:09:38.130
And so, it happens, things change.

01:09:38.450 --> 01:09:40.060
You lose opportunities.

01:09:40.060 --> 01:09:43.690
While you have a chance
to do a three-day retreat,

01:09:43.690 --> 01:09:46.660
for God's sake, do a good one.

01:09:46.660 --> 01:09:49.550
Take the time. Take the chance. Do it.

01:09:49.550 --> 01:09:51.840
And do that retreat.

01:09:51.840 --> 01:09:54.330
What's the last one?

01:09:54.330 --> 01:09:57.200
Yeah dedicate the good karma,

01:09:57.200 --> 01:09:58.730
like give it away to people.

01:09:58.730 --> 01:10:00.360
I can't avoid

01:10:02.440 --> 01:10:06.420
the image in my mind of a fire offering.

01:10:06.420 --> 01:10:11.320
When we do fire offerings,
like at Diamond Mountain,

01:10:11.320 --> 01:10:15.300
when the smoke goes out to the sky

01:10:15.300 --> 01:10:17.130
and the wind blows it away,

01:10:17.130 --> 01:10:20.050
I always imagine that sooner or later

01:10:20.050 --> 01:10:21.930
it will touch everyone.

01:10:21.930 --> 01:10:25.890
That mini pollution will sooner or later,

01:10:25.890 --> 01:10:30.890
the particles of the offerings
during the fire offering

01:10:31.310 --> 01:10:35.040
will reach all beings and do some kind of

01:10:35.040 --> 01:10:39.000
imagine the good karma
being sent out like that.

01:10:39.000 --> 01:10:40.493
And that's all.

01:10:44.210 --> 01:10:46.640
What I'm saying it's hard
work, especially studying,

01:10:46.640 --> 01:10:49.035
oh, one more thing.

01:10:51.165 --> 01:10:56.165
Kamalashila, in the Stages of Meditation,

01:10:56.370 --> 01:10:59.623
he rushes through

01:10:59.623 --> 01:11:04.623
the actual stages, the
nine levels of meditation

01:11:04.740 --> 01:11:07.918
and the five antidotes,

01:11:07.918 --> 01:11:10.324
the eight,

01:11:10.324 --> 01:11:12.410
the eight antidotes and the five problems.

01:11:12.410 --> 01:11:14.083
He rushes through that.

01:11:14.083 --> 01:11:17.840
I was like waiting for him,

01:11:17.840 --> 01:11:20.940
I thought he would, his
book's kind of long.

01:11:20.940 --> 01:11:24.440
So I thought, wow, he's
going to give some detail.

01:11:24.440 --> 01:11:27.640
He doesn't. He rushes
through all the stuff

01:11:27.640 --> 01:11:29.550
that's on the chart.

01:11:29.550 --> 01:11:33.130
and then he spends like 20 pages on

01:11:34.583 --> 01:11:37.500
SO SOR RNAM PAR RTOG PA

01:11:42.540 --> 01:11:43.933
which means,

01:11:47.310 --> 01:11:50.330
cogitating, in English.

01:11:50.330 --> 01:11:54.980
Cogitating means to sit
in your meditation cabin.

01:11:54.980 --> 01:11:56.100
Right, Connie?

01:11:56.100 --> 01:11:58.976
For three years, three
months and three days

01:11:58.976 --> 01:12:01.767
And just think about stuff.

01:12:01.767 --> 01:12:05.550
Just thinking about why stuff empty

01:12:05.550 --> 01:12:08.360
and don't forget
Kamalashila went to Tibet.

01:12:08.360 --> 01:12:12.690
He and his teacher were involved
with these intense debates

01:12:12.690 --> 01:12:15.040
with other practitioners

01:12:15.040 --> 01:12:19.110
about the usefulness of
thinking about nothing.

01:12:19.110 --> 01:12:23.157
There was even some intrigue.
Somebody was murdered.

01:12:23.157 --> 01:12:28.157
And it got hot and don't
forget he was in this,

01:12:29.700 --> 01:12:31.960
he was there

01:12:31.960 --> 01:12:36.960
and so he spends about
200 pages in English,

01:12:39.730 --> 01:12:43.403
defending thinking about emptiness.

01:12:44.600 --> 01:12:48.810
He spends about 200 pages defending

01:12:50.220 --> 01:12:52.990
trying to figure out
emptiness from the books.

01:12:54.360 --> 01:12:58.930
He says, you have to. He
says it's not a luxury

01:12:58.930 --> 01:13:01.780
and it's not some scholarly thing.

01:13:01.780 --> 01:13:05.590
And it's not boring
and it's not difficult,

01:13:05.590 --> 01:13:07.580
and it's not technical.

01:13:07.580 --> 01:13:11.850
It's the only way to
see emptiness directly.

01:13:11.850 --> 01:13:15.040
He goes on for,

01:13:15.040 --> 01:13:16.150
in English it would be,

01:13:16.150 --> 01:13:20.340
I dunno, almost 200 pages in English.

01:13:20.340 --> 01:13:22.600
He's just keep repeating the same thing

01:13:22.600 --> 01:13:23.950
over and over again.

01:13:23.950 --> 01:13:27.610
You have to struggle

01:13:27.610 --> 01:13:29.260
in meditation

01:13:29.260 --> 01:13:32.250
to understand about emptiness.

01:13:32.250 --> 01:13:35.390
Then it will turn into
the direct perception,

01:13:35.390 --> 01:13:37.610
that will turn into the direct perception.

01:13:37.610 --> 01:13:40.040
You got to get all this Mixed Nuts books.

01:13:40.040 --> 01:13:41.920
You got to struggle through them.

01:13:41.920 --> 01:13:45.640
You got to try and understand
the 38 proofs of emptiness.

01:13:45.640 --> 01:13:50.590
You must do that struggle
and he says, without that,

01:13:50.590 --> 01:13:51.960
forget it.

01:13:51.960 --> 01:13:54.813
Then the last thing he says,
okay and then we can stop.

01:13:55.980 --> 01:14:00.740
He says, you know when in Boy Scouts

01:14:00.740 --> 01:14:04.330
or when they teach you
to rub sticks together

01:14:04.330 --> 01:14:07.680
and make a fire, God, you don't
know how many days we spent

01:14:07.680 --> 01:14:10.430
trying to do that in Boy Scouts.

01:14:10.430 --> 01:14:13.713
It is possible but it's difficult.

01:14:15.370 --> 01:14:19.399
You can do it with a bow and a string

01:14:19.399 --> 01:14:20.570
and a bowl,

01:14:20.570 --> 01:14:25.570
and certain kinds of
shavings from certain plants.

01:14:25.640 --> 01:14:27.540
You can do it. I've done it

01:14:27.540 --> 01:14:30.380
but it takes about four
hours or something.

01:14:30.380 --> 01:14:33.290
A match is much easier.

01:14:33.290 --> 01:14:37.780
We always had matches
hidden in our pockets.

01:14:37.780 --> 01:14:42.490
Then he says, I tell you something,

01:14:42.490 --> 01:14:44.120
struggle, struggle, struggle for hours

01:14:44.120 --> 01:14:46.030
with these stupid two sticks,

01:14:46.030 --> 01:14:48.280
and then he says, you
know it's really fun is

01:14:49.766 --> 01:14:52.630
to throw the stick in
the fire first thing.

01:14:52.630 --> 01:14:56.824
Once you get the fire
going, throw the stick in.

01:14:56.824 --> 01:15:00.070
Then he's like, okay, see you guys later.

01:15:00.070 --> 01:15:02.340
Then we're like, what?

01:15:02.340 --> 01:15:04.150
Yeah, got it.

01:15:04.150 --> 01:15:05.390
Well, yeah, yeah,

01:15:05.390 --> 01:15:07.880
You use the stick, blah,
blah, blah, make the fire

01:15:07.880 --> 01:15:10.880
and then throw the goddamn
stick in a fire and burn it up.

01:15:10.880 --> 01:15:13.200
What he means is

01:15:13.200 --> 01:15:16.220
there is a state of non-conceptual,

01:15:16.220 --> 01:15:19.050
direct perception of emptiness

01:15:19.050 --> 01:15:20.870
but the way you get there

01:15:20.870 --> 01:15:25.870
is through thousands of
hours of conceptual thinking.

01:15:25.958 --> 01:15:28.890
It's like the stick that makes the fire.

01:15:28.890 --> 01:15:32.353
Then okay you can throw
the stick in the fire

01:15:32.353 --> 01:15:34.120
and it will burn up,

01:15:34.120 --> 01:15:37.430
in the fire of direct
perception of emptiness.

01:15:37.430 --> 01:15:39.640
But you can't make it without the stick.

01:15:39.640 --> 01:15:41.470
You can't make that
fire without the stick.

01:15:41.470 --> 01:15:42.890
It's a very beautiful image.

01:15:42.890 --> 01:15:44.700
It's a very, very beautiful image.

01:15:44.700 --> 01:15:48.640
And by the way, that's where he says,

01:15:48.640 --> 01:15:51.860
he says in Sanskrit,

01:15:51.860 --> 01:15:54.748
I think it's DVAYAM or something.

01:15:54.748 --> 01:15:59.648
%DVAYAM BHUMI ASHWA PASHYET DUAVAT - $1000

01:16:04.220 --> 01:16:06.470
No, I'm not serious.

01:16:06.470 --> 01:16:10.383
Show the horse the course
before you run the race.

01:16:12.170 --> 01:16:15.700
It comes from him, I didn't know that.

01:16:15.700 --> 01:16:18.690
You don't take a horse out for a race

01:16:18.690 --> 01:16:21.560
without showing them the track first,

01:16:21.560 --> 01:16:23.830
riding around the track
for a couple of days

01:16:23.830 --> 01:16:26.660
and then you go on the race.

01:16:26.660 --> 01:16:29.450
So it's like read the books on emptiness,

01:16:29.450 --> 01:16:33.393
study them deeply, and then run your race.

01:16:34.430 --> 01:16:36.670
Now what's the,

01:16:36.670 --> 01:16:38.540
what are we doing with
the OM MANI PADME HUNG?

01:16:38.540 --> 01:16:41.085
It's very simple.

01:16:42.960 --> 01:16:44.020
I also used to,

01:16:44.020 --> 01:16:45.280
okay, this is the whole stories

01:16:45.280 --> 01:16:47.780
of things I didn't
believe from my teacher.

01:16:47.780 --> 01:16:50.924
He said, I'll do this
mantra a thousand times,

01:16:50.924 --> 01:16:54.053
or I'll do it 10,000 times
or do it 100,000 times.

01:16:55.770 --> 01:16:58.780
Lock yourself in a room
and do this mantra.

01:16:58.780 --> 01:17:01.500
And I was like,

01:17:01.500 --> 01:17:03.510
yeah, okay, I'll get to that.

01:17:03.510 --> 01:17:06.100
That was my thing with my teacher.

01:17:06.100 --> 01:17:08.190
I learned that you're
not supposed to say no.

01:17:08.190 --> 01:17:10.730
You just can delay.

01:17:10.730 --> 01:17:11.840
I'll say, oh yeah,

01:17:11.840 --> 01:17:15.530
as soon as I get some
couple of weeks off of work,

01:17:15.530 --> 01:17:17.870
I definitely lock myself in a room

01:17:17.870 --> 01:17:20.000
and say OM MANI PADME HUNGs.

01:17:20.000 --> 01:17:22.290
It's on my list of things to do,

01:17:22.290 --> 01:17:25.400
bucket list before I die.

01:17:26.610 --> 01:17:30.030
Then he went on a trip to Europe

01:17:30.030 --> 01:17:33.610
to see Jampel Sangye was
his name, %Tuchi's teacher,

01:17:33.610 --> 01:17:35.660
he went to go see him in Rome.

01:17:35.660 --> 01:17:38.590
So I was kind of stuck in the house alone

01:17:38.590 --> 01:17:41.280
and I said, well, he's
got this guest room.

01:17:41.280 --> 01:17:44.260
And I had another monk with
me and he said, I'll cook

01:17:44.260 --> 01:17:46.310
if you want to say mantras.

01:17:46.310 --> 01:17:48.250
So I said, yeah.

01:17:48.250 --> 01:17:51.370
So I went in Rinpoche's guest room,

01:17:51.370 --> 01:17:54.088
which I built,

01:17:55.350 --> 01:17:57.500
and I did a two, three week retreat

01:17:57.500 --> 01:18:00.270
and I just did OM MANI PADME HUNGs.

01:18:00.270 --> 01:18:04.046
It's a very, very powerful mantra

01:18:04.046 --> 01:18:05.720
and I don't think a lot of people

01:18:05.720 --> 01:18:07.920
understand the meaning of the mantra.

01:18:07.920 --> 01:18:11.950
But OM is called %SGO 'BYED

01:18:11.950 --> 01:18:14.890
which means the door
that opens to the mantra.

01:18:16.282 --> 01:18:19.610
So OM is the door of the mantra

01:18:19.610 --> 01:18:23.780
and then HUNG at the end is, %GZER BTZUGS

01:18:23.780 --> 01:18:27.530
which means to stick the sacred dagger

01:18:27.530 --> 01:18:31.095
in the ground and say, "May
it be so." HUNG means that.

01:18:31.095 --> 01:18:35.570
So OM is like, I'm about to say a mantra

01:18:35.570 --> 01:18:37.290
and then HUNG is like, goddamn.

01:18:38.598 --> 01:18:43.598
So between that, it's just MANI PADME

01:18:45.546 --> 01:18:50.546
and MANI means a gem, gemstone,

01:18:51.418 --> 01:18:52.500
a jewel.

01:18:52.500 --> 01:18:56.020
It's funny because it sounds like money,

01:18:56.020 --> 01:19:00.140
which you need to buy a jewel

01:19:00.140 --> 01:19:04.760
Then PADMA means a Lotus flower

01:19:06.780 --> 01:19:11.780
It's very important that it's PADME.

01:19:11.840 --> 01:19:16.320
which John will tell you is
the, which case? The locative.

01:19:17.550 --> 01:19:19.270
Yeah, in the lotus.

01:19:19.270 --> 01:19:20.440
The jewel in the lotus.

01:19:20.440 --> 01:19:24.000
So it's not just jewel lotus.

01:19:24.000 --> 01:19:26.530
It's jewel in the lotus

01:19:26.530 --> 01:19:28.880
And it's a reference to tantra.

01:19:28.880 --> 01:19:30.327
It's a direct reference to tantra.

01:19:30.327 --> 01:19:35.271
Tt's funny that it's a mantra.

01:19:36.260 --> 01:19:39.800
If you're the kind of person
who believes it's possible

01:19:39.800 --> 01:19:43.410
that your spiritual
partner could be a Buddha,

01:19:43.410 --> 01:19:45.820
then it's very important to you.

01:19:45.820 --> 01:19:47.780
And the people who criticize that

01:19:47.780 --> 01:19:52.570
are doing OM MANI PADME
HUNG all day. It's so funny

01:19:52.570 --> 01:19:55.252
because it means have a spiritual partner.

01:19:55.252 --> 01:19:58.090
It's so funny that

01:19:58.090 --> 01:20:00.120
the people who criticize the practice

01:20:00.120 --> 01:20:04.430
of a spiritual partner, which
Buddha followed and taught,

01:20:05.830 --> 01:20:09.200
say, Well, let's go do OM
MANI PADME HUNGs instead.

01:20:09.200 --> 01:20:11.370
But OM MANI PADME HUNG means

01:20:11.370 --> 01:20:14.770
I hope I meet my partner.
And it's funny. It just,

01:20:14.770 --> 01:20:15.603
to me, it's funny.

01:20:15.603 --> 01:20:18.090
But anyway.

01:20:18.090 --> 01:20:22.630
So you can think of that jewel

01:20:22.630 --> 01:20:25.750
as love and bodhichitta.

01:20:25.750 --> 01:20:28.595
And you can think of the PADME

01:20:28.595 --> 01:20:31.560
as inserting it into

01:20:31.560 --> 01:20:33.220
understanding of emptiness.

01:20:33.220 --> 01:20:36.600
So if you can, I like
to call it a marriage

01:20:37.710 --> 01:20:41.890
of emptiness and compassion,
or a marriage of emptiness

01:20:41.890 --> 01:20:46.830
and love for other people.

01:20:46.830 --> 01:20:48.930
Then that's perfection

01:20:48.930 --> 01:20:50.730
And that's Buddhahood.

01:20:50.730 --> 01:20:55.730
So try to put your
compassion into emptiness

01:20:56.160 --> 01:20:58.650
and that's OM MANI PADME HUNG.

01:20:58.650 --> 01:21:03.650
So if you understand a little
bit about it and you do,

01:21:04.020 --> 01:21:05.900
I would try to do 10,000.

01:21:05.900 --> 01:21:08.520
Sometimes you can try to do 100,000.

01:21:08.520 --> 01:21:13.520
Itt's not stupid to count
them. That's another myth.

01:21:13.840 --> 01:21:15.940
It's very cool to count them.

01:21:15.940 --> 01:21:18.190
And it's cool to reach 10,000.

01:21:18.190 --> 01:21:20.330
And it's cool to reach 100,000.

01:21:20.330 --> 01:21:22.500
And things happen at 10,000

01:21:22.500 --> 01:21:27.250
that don't happen at
9,999. I'm telling you.

01:21:27.250 --> 01:21:30.010
So set yourself a goal and get a rosary,

01:21:30.010 --> 01:21:33.640
and try to do and keep track.

01:21:33.640 --> 01:21:38.640
I keep hash mark: one, two,
three, [four] and then cross.

01:21:39.097 --> 01:21:42.080
Five. Five hundred like that.

01:21:42.080 --> 01:21:44.730
So keep it, actually keep a count

01:21:44.730 --> 01:21:46.730
of how many do.

01:21:46.730 --> 01:21:49.160
And it works. It really does work.

01:21:49.160 --> 01:21:52.150
Trust me, I thought it was stupid

01:21:52.150 --> 01:21:53.880
and I thought it was a waste of time,

01:21:53.880 --> 01:21:56.550
and I thought it was
superstitious. And it's not.

01:21:56.550 --> 01:21:58.920
It's a very, very powerful
and very beautiful.

01:21:58.920 --> 01:22:02.113
So try to do three days of mantras.

01:22:03.850 --> 01:22:05.180
You're supposed to not rush them.

01:22:05.180 --> 01:22:09.180
You're supposed to say them
clearly or it doesn't work.

01:22:09.180 --> 01:22:10.590
It doesn't work as well.

01:22:10.590 --> 01:22:14.090
So don't rush them so
fast that you're like,

01:22:14.090 --> 01:22:19.067
but (speaks too fast to
understand anything).

01:22:20.250 --> 01:22:24.122
Try to use the third
finger of your left hand

01:22:24.122 --> 01:22:28.841
and that has a special prana.
And it's more powerful.

01:22:28.841 --> 01:22:32.810
It's uncomfortable for the first few days

01:22:32.810 --> 01:22:37.490
but hold your rosary here.

01:22:37.490 --> 01:22:39.690
okay, last story, grandpa's last story.

01:22:39.690 --> 01:22:41.890
I was in a train station in India

01:22:41.890 --> 01:22:46.040
and I was with a couple of hippie friends

01:22:46.040 --> 01:22:47.720
and we didn't know anything.

01:22:47.720 --> 01:22:52.720
We saw these Tibetans rushing
in to a little side room

01:22:53.960 --> 01:22:55.650
and we're like, hey,
what's going on in there?

01:22:55.650 --> 01:22:59.180
And they said, Ling Rinpoche is there,

01:22:59.180 --> 01:23:03.890
the senior tutor. He's sitting in there.

01:23:03.890 --> 01:23:08.490
And I'm like, wow, that's cool, man.

01:23:08.490 --> 01:23:09.323
Can we meet him?

01:23:09.323 --> 01:23:12.790
And they said, well, you can try.

01:23:12.790 --> 01:23:15.670
And they said, normally you
got to have an offering.

01:23:15.670 --> 01:23:17.180
So we run across the street,

01:23:17.180 --> 01:23:22.180
we bought this crummy
little cake at a bake shop.

01:23:22.900 --> 01:23:26.470
We rushed back to the waiting room

01:23:26.470 --> 01:23:28.210
and he's in there, and the train's coming

01:23:28.210 --> 01:23:31.090
and we said we got the cake.

01:23:31.090 --> 01:23:32.680
We can come in?

01:23:32.680 --> 01:23:36.800
Then I can go in and we met him.

01:23:36.800 --> 01:23:39.350
We had an extraordinary meeting

01:23:39.350 --> 01:23:42.448
but he was going like this the whole time

01:23:42.448 --> 01:23:44.093
and he didn't have rosary.

01:23:48.026 --> 01:23:49.490
He did so many mantras that

01:23:49.490 --> 01:23:54.030
he decided he didn't
need the rosary anymore.

01:23:54.030 --> 01:23:57.000
So he would just be like this all day

01:23:57.000 --> 01:23:58.360
It was kind of a weird thing

01:23:58.360 --> 01:24:00.260
we're like, what's going on with his hand?

01:24:00.260 --> 01:24:02.790
And they are like, he's doing mantras.

01:24:02.790 --> 01:24:04.163
I said does he need a rosary?

01:24:04.163 --> 01:24:05.490
I could go buy one.

01:24:05.490 --> 01:24:09.950
They said, nah he doesn't
even want anymore.

01:24:09.950 --> 01:24:12.920
So do your mantras and enjoy.

01:24:12.920 --> 01:24:15.716
And work hard.

01:24:15.716 --> 01:24:17.390
When you work hard,

01:24:17.390 --> 01:24:21.590
when you study things you don't
understand, you learn more.

01:24:21.590 --> 01:24:23.890
When you study things, you do understand,

01:24:23.890 --> 01:24:24.950
you don't learn as much.

01:24:24.950 --> 01:24:27.050
Okay, all right see you guys later.

01:24:27.050 --> 01:24:29.243
Good luck on your retreat. Thank you.

